window.CET6_BANKS.push({"id": "2022-12-1", "source": "2022年12月真题·第1套", "writing": {"prompt": "Directions: For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write an essay that begins with the sentence“With the application of information technology in education, college students can now learn in more diverse and efficient ways.” You can make statements, give reasons, or cite examples to develop your essay. You should write at least 150 words but no more than 200 words.", "sample": "With the application of information technology in education, college students can now learn in more diverse\nand efficient ways. Not long ago, learning was confined to a fixed classroom and a single textbook, but\ntechnology has broken these limits and reshaped how we acquire knowledge.\nOn the one hand, learning has become far more diverse. Through massive open online courses, a student in a\nsmall town can now attend lectures delivered by professors at top universities, which was once unthinkable,\nand digital libraries offer millions of books and papers at the click of a button. On the other hand, learning is\nremarkably efficient. Thanks to AI-powered tutors, questions that once took days to solve can be answered in\nseconds, and search engines help us locate exactly the material we need. As a result, we save time and study\nwith greater focus.\nIn conclusion, information technology has enriched both the variety and the speed of learning. Yet we should\nuse these tools wisely, treating them as aids to independent thinking rather than substitutes for it."}, "translation": {"prompt": "青藏高原(the Qinghai-Tibet Plateau)位于中国西南部，面积约230万平方公里，平均海拔4000米以上，被称为\"世界屋脊\"。青藏高原自然资源丰富，风景秀丽，拥有多种珍稀野生动物。 青藏高原气温很低，形成了大面积高山冰川。这里是亚洲许多著名河流的源头，是中国和东南亚的主要淡水供应源。青藏高原对全球生态系统至关重要。 由于气候变化的影响，青藏高原的冰川正在加速融化。中国一直在努力保护青藏高原的生态系统，草地覆盖率不断增加，许多濒危物种得到更为有效的保护。", "sample": "Located in the southwest of China, the Qinghai-Tibet Plateau, with an area of about 2.3 million square kilometers and an average altitude of over 4,000 meters, is known as \"the Roof of the World\". It is rich in natural resources, boasts beautiful scenery, and is home to various rare wild animals. Due to its low temperatures, the plateau has formed large areas of alpine glaciers. It is the source of many famous rivers in Asia and a major freshwater supply for China and Southeast Asia. It is vital to the global ecosystem. Due to climate change, the glaciers on the plateau are melting at an accelerating rate. China has been making efforts to protect the ecosystem of the plateau, with grassland coverage steadily increasing and many endangered species being more effectively protected."}, "listeningUrl": "https://english-exam.lazynote.cn/cet6/paper/2022-12-1/?f=w", "clozePassage": "During the summer, when I was a visiting poet at a residency out of state, an angry, confused woman wandered into my class and said: \"I have three guns and I want to use them.\" We all  __26__  . It wasn't clear if she had the guns, but we each know that, when we teach in America, we are already in danger.\nI was dizzy with fear. The woman, who later turned out to be a schizophrenic(精神分裂症患者) without  __27__  to her medications, was, by some force, wrestled out and  __28__  away, then put in a hospital for observation, in a step that was actually safer for everyone than any one of us pressing charges. My class went on; we talked about poems. But despite the fact that the rest of our days on campus passed  __29__  , I was rattled. I couldn't shake the sense that in this country we always live at  __30__  risk.\nA few months later, crisis  __31__  again. While my husband was locking his bike to drop off our 3-year-old daughter for her preschool-aged day camp, a different woman approached. Swiftly and for no  __32__  reason, she bent down, picked up our daughter, and began to carry her down the street. It was so fast and confusing that my daughter  __33__  cried. My husband, in a burst of speed, chased the woman and reclaimed our daughter. The woman, clearly confused, retreated into the public library. A  __34__  of homeless people who generally know the other homeless in the area said they did not recognize the woman. The woman was so clearly unwell that when she was taken into custody she was incoherent. Heartbreakingly, she called our daughter by the name of someone else's child. Each part of the episode was as haunting as it was  __35__  .", "matchIntro": "This man is running 7 marathons on 7 continents in 7 days", "matchParagraphs": [{"label": "A", "text": "Michael Wardian pushed forward into the penetrating arctic(北极的) wind, fighting the urge to speed up. Too much effort and he'd begin to sweat, which, he was told, would only increase the risk of hypothermia(体温过低)."}, {"label": "B", "text": "At the 2014 North Pole Marathon, the temperature dipped to minus-22 degrees F, with a wind chill that made it feel even colder. Along the route, armed guards wandered the large sheets of floating ice to minimize the risk of polar bear attacks."}, {"label": "C", "text": "\"I like to do stuff that scares me,\" Wardian said. With ice frozen to his beard, Wardian crossed the finish line that April afternoon in a winning time of 4 hours 7 minutes and 40 seconds, almost two hours slower than his personal best over 26.2 miles. The race for Wardian, however, was less about the result than overcoming his aversion to the cold."}, {"label": "D", "text": "In a few days, Wardian will once again compete in an unfamiliar territory and below-freezing temperatures. He will line up Monday in Antarctica(南极) for the first leg of the World Marathon Challenge—joining 32 other adventure seekers on an unusual journey where participants travel through different time zones and climates to run seven marathons on seven continents in seven days."}, {"label": "E", "text": "An elite ultra-runner, Wardian has his sights on breaking the event's record average marathon time of 3:32:25 set last January by U.S. Marine Corps captain Daniel Cartica. Wardian, a 42-year-old Arlington resident, is a record-breaking racer, known in the ultra-running community for seeking tough courses and setting world records. Last year, he ran 1,254.65 miles in 47 races. The World Marathon Challenge, like most of Wardian's running goals, will be about pushing his limits. \"I love diverse and unique challenges,\" he said. \"I'm definitely interested in seeing what I can handle and what my body can accept. That drives me.\""}, {"label": "F", "text": "Something about the way Richard Donovan carried himself appealed to Wardian. Perhaps it was the sense of adventure Donovan displayed when they first met at the 2010 50K Championships in Galway, Ireland, where Donovan was the race director. The two hit it off, and soon Wardian was participating in Donovan's events. It was at the North Pole Marathon, a race that Donovan organizes, that Wardian first heard about the Irishman's plan for the World Marathon Challenge—a challenge that Donovan himself completed in 2009 and 2012. \"I knew that many people had a goal of running seven marathons on seven continents during any time period,\" Donovan, 50, said. \"I felt the natural extension to this idea would be to try to achieve it within a seven-day period.\""}, {"label": "G", "text": "Wardian started saving for the trip in 2014, connecting with sponsors and getting approval from his wife, Jennifer, before committing. Registration for the event costs 36,000 euros, which covers international charter flights to each of the seven marathon locations: Union Glacier (Antarctica), Punta Arenas, Chile (South America), Miami (North America), Madrid (Europe), Marrakesh, Morocco (Africa), Dubai (Asia) and Sydney (Australia). The challenge is a test of both physical strength and mental fitness. Sleeping on a crammed plane, adjusting to different time zones and finding food to eat (Wardian is a vegetarian) would make it an exhausting trip over a month, let alone a week. \"The key to a race like this is getting comfortable being uncomfortable,\" said Becca Pizzi, last year's women's champion. \"The highs of the race are incredibly high, and the lows incredibly low.\""}, {"label": "H", "text": "Since turning it into an organized event in 2015, Donovan has attracted a variety of runners. This year's challenge will feature a far more elite field, which includes Ryan Hall, America's fastest marathon runner. Despite his proven track record, Hall said he has no time goals and that he still suffers from the same fatigue issues that forced him to leave the professional ranks in 2015. Hall plans to run with his friend, Pastor Matthew Barnett of The Dream Center in Los Angeles—one of the six American men who will be competing. \"I don't expect to run a step with Mike, but I will be excited to see how he does,\" said the 34-year-old Hall, who began weight-lifting after retiring. \"If I finish within an hour of him in each marathon, I'd be surprised.\""}, {"label": "I", "text": "Instead, 43-year-old Petr Vabrousek, an elite Czech Ironman champion, is expected to be Wardian's closest challenger. To others on the trip, simply finishing will be its own reward. Sinead Kane of Ireland is aiming to become the first blind person to complete the challenge. And Beth Ann Telford, a 47-year-old federal government worker from Fairfax and the only American female in this year's mix, is using the event as a platform to raise money for cancer research. It's a cause with a personal connection to Telford, who was diagnosed with brain cancer in 2004. \"Doing something like this is definitely the hardest challenge that I've ever done except for the chemotherapy and brain surgery,\" she said. \"It's going to raise awareness. …I just wanted to do something that is epic and this certainly is right up there.\" Wardian, too, hopes his involvement will give him a platform to promote a cause. He recently became an ambassador for the United Nations Women's HeForShe initiative to fight inequalities faced by women and girls worldwide."}, {"label": "J", "text": "On a chilly December afternoon, Wardian wove through Washington's crowded sidewalks on the way home from his full-time job as an international ship broker. His elastic, 6-foot frame bounced gently and efficiently off the ground with each step of the hilly six-mile trip back to Arlington. This is a daily routine during the week for Wardian, who started racing professionally in 2003 and runs seven days a week, often multiple times a day. When he travels, he prefers to explore new places on his feet."}, {"label": "K", "text": "But in some ways, Wardian still has trouble thinking of himself as a runner. For the majority of his childhood, Wardian devoted his energy to becoming a Division I lacrosse(长曲棍球) player-a dream he realized when he was recruited to play at Michigan State University. \"Once he decides to do something, he just works at it until he does it,\" Michael's younger sister, Mariele, said. \"Once he decides to do it, it's usually something that's going to happen. He's always been like that. He's a very motivated individual.\""}, {"label": "L", "text": "It was only a year or so ago that Wardian realized that he had been a runner longer than a lacrosse player. It was not until he ran in the 2004 U.S. Olympic Marathon Trials-the first of three for Wardian-that he felt that he was a legitimate runner. Now more than 10 years and numerous ultra-marathon national titles and world records later, he embraces that identity. Wardian wants to see how far his legs can take him, one epic challenge at a time. \"I want to always keep doing things that are exciting, adventurous, different and most importantly, probably things I'm not the best at,\" Wardian said, \"because if you're not seeking things out that are challenging and difficult for you, then you're not growing … So I hope maybe people see what I do, and say, 'Okay, I want to do something different or try something new. … I'm going to do something that scares me.' That's what I'm hoping people will take from it.\""}], "readingPassages": {"46": "Many people associate their self-worth with their work. The more successful their career, the better they feel about themselves. Work-related self-esteem is therefore a worthy ideal to pursue with vigor, right? Well, not always. According to recent research, in which psychologists interviewed 370 full-time workers over a period of three weeks, the reality is a little more complicated. And it involves negative as well as positive consequences.\nIt's natural to be drawn towards pleasure and to step away from pain. In the workplace, if that pleasure comes from a triumph which swells our self-respect, people will try to repeat the accomplishment. But repeating that accomplishment is often not realistic, which can lead to severe negative emotional consequences when it doesn't reoccur. This form of motivation is widely regarded as a negative type of motivation. It can hinder other more positive motivation types, such as completing a task purely because it's fulfilling or enjoyable.\nWhat consumes the employee instead is a pressing need to feel mighty and sure of themselves. They then take on only tasks and objectives which serve that ego-driven need. As a result, to avoid feelings of shame and worthlessness associated with failure, they extend themselves to such a degree that there's a subsequent adverse effect on their well-being. This internal pressure to succeed at all costs demands a lot of effort. It depletes their energy, culminating in disproportionate levels of damaging sentiment.\nThose negative emotions mount into heightened anxiety, impacting their ability to make the most of their personal life. Their desire to avoid feeling inferior ends up making them feel inferior when it comes to their diminished capacity for friendship and leisure. They end up dissatisfied both at work and outside of it.\nBut thankfully, for those people compelled almost entirely by this specific form of motivation, the news isn't all bad, or bad at all. The study also discovered several positive outcomes that can actually outweigh the harmful ones. Though these types of employees are motivated by the desire to avoid negative consequences, they are also motivated by the excitement of pursuing emotional rewards. This excitement makes pursuing goals enjoyable and stimulates pleasure and pride that would result from success. An effect of the positive motivation is that it neutralizes the existence of negative motivation.\nSure, it affects people's personal lives to what could be deemed an unhealthy extent, because leisure activities are often seen as a part of life that must be sacrificed to manage work and family demands. However, the way people feel about their work has less to do with whether they're motivated by the preservation of self-esteem but more with the fact that they're simply motivated.", "47": "Many people associate their self-worth with their work. The more successful their career, the better they feel about themselves. Work-related self-esteem is therefore a worthy ideal to pursue with vigor, right? Well, not always. According to recent research, in which psychologists interviewed 370 full-time workers over a period of three weeks, the reality is a little more complicated. And it involves negative as well as positive consequences.\nIt's natural to be drawn towards pleasure and to step away from pain. In the workplace, if that pleasure comes from a triumph which swells our self-respect, people will try to repeat the accomplishment. But repeating that accomplishment is often not realistic, which can lead to severe negative emotional consequences when it doesn't reoccur. This form of motivation is widely regarded as a negative type of motivation. It can hinder other more positive motivation types, such as completing a task purely because it's fulfilling or enjoyable.\nWhat consumes the employee instead is a pressing need to feel mighty and sure of themselves. They then take on only tasks and objectives which serve that ego-driven need. As a result, to avoid feelings of shame and worthlessness associated with failure, they extend themselves to such a degree that there's a subsequent adverse effect on their well-being. This internal pressure to succeed at all costs demands a lot of effort. It depletes their energy, culminating in disproportionate levels of damaging sentiment.\nThose negative emotions mount into heightened anxiety, impacting their ability to make the most of their personal life. Their desire to avoid feeling inferior ends up making them feel inferior when it comes to their diminished capacity for friendship and leisure. They end up dissatisfied both at work and outside of it.\nBut thankfully, for those people compelled almost entirely by this specific form of motivation, the news isn't all bad, or bad at all. The study also discovered several positive outcomes that can actually outweigh the harmful ones. Though these types of employees are motivated by the desire to avoid negative consequences, they are also motivated by the excitement of pursuing emotional rewards. This excitement makes pursuing goals enjoyable and stimulates pleasure and pride that would result from success. An effect of the positive motivation is that it neutralizes the existence of negative motivation.\nSure, it affects people's personal lives to what could be deemed an unhealthy extent, because leisure activities are often seen as a part of life that must be sacrificed to manage work and family demands. However, the way people feel about their work has less to do with whether they're motivated by the preservation of self-esteem but more with the fact that they're simply motivated.", "48": "Many people associate their self-worth with their work. The more successful their career, the better they feel about themselves. Work-related self-esteem is therefore a worthy ideal to pursue with vigor, right? Well, not always. According to recent research, in which psychologists interviewed 370 full-time workers over a period of three weeks, the reality is a little more complicated. And it involves negative as well as positive consequences.\nIt's natural to be drawn towards pleasure and to step away from pain. In the workplace, if that pleasure comes from a triumph which swells our self-respect, people will try to repeat the accomplishment. But repeating that accomplishment is often not realistic, which can lead to severe negative emotional consequences when it doesn't reoccur. This form of motivation is widely regarded as a negative type of motivation. It can hinder other more positive motivation types, such as completing a task purely because it's fulfilling or enjoyable.\nWhat consumes the employee instead is a pressing need to feel mighty and sure of themselves. They then take on only tasks and objectives which serve that ego-driven need. As a result, to avoid feelings of shame and worthlessness associated with failure, they extend themselves to such a degree that there's a subsequent adverse effect on their well-being. This internal pressure to succeed at all costs demands a lot of effort. It depletes their energy, culminating in disproportionate levels of damaging sentiment.\nThose negative emotions mount into heightened anxiety, impacting their ability to make the most of their personal life. Their desire to avoid feeling inferior ends up making them feel inferior when it comes to their diminished capacity for friendship and leisure. They end up dissatisfied both at work and outside of it.\nBut thankfully, for those people compelled almost entirely by this specific form of motivation, the news isn't all bad, or bad at all. The study also discovered several positive outcomes that can actually outweigh the harmful ones. Though these types of employees are motivated by the desire to avoid negative consequences, they are also motivated by the excitement of pursuing emotional rewards. This excitement makes pursuing goals enjoyable and stimulates pleasure and pride that would result from success. An effect of the positive motivation is that it neutralizes the existence of negative motivation.\nSure, it affects people's personal lives to what could be deemed an unhealthy extent, because leisure activities are often seen as a part of life that must be sacrificed to manage work and family demands. However, the way people feel about their work has less to do with whether they're motivated by the preservation of self-esteem but more with the fact that they're simply motivated.", "49": "Many people associate their self-worth with their work. The more successful their career, the better they feel about themselves. Work-related self-esteem is therefore a worthy ideal to pursue with vigor, right? Well, not always. According to recent research, in which psychologists interviewed 370 full-time workers over a period of three weeks, the reality is a little more complicated. And it involves negative as well as positive consequences.\nIt's natural to be drawn towards pleasure and to step away from pain. In the workplace, if that pleasure comes from a triumph which swells our self-respect, people will try to repeat the accomplishment. But repeating that accomplishment is often not realistic, which can lead to severe negative emotional consequences when it doesn't reoccur. This form of motivation is widely regarded as a negative type of motivation. It can hinder other more positive motivation types, such as completing a task purely because it's fulfilling or enjoyable.\nWhat consumes the employee instead is a pressing need to feel mighty and sure of themselves. They then take on only tasks and objectives which serve that ego-driven need. As a result, to avoid feelings of shame and worthlessness associated with failure, they extend themselves to such a degree that there's a subsequent adverse effect on their well-being. This internal pressure to succeed at all costs demands a lot of effort. It depletes their energy, culminating in disproportionate levels of damaging sentiment.\nThose negative emotions mount into heightened anxiety, impacting their ability to make the most of their personal life. Their desire to avoid feeling inferior ends up making them feel inferior when it comes to their diminished capacity for friendship and leisure. They end up dissatisfied both at work and outside of it.\nBut thankfully, for those people compelled almost entirely by this specific form of motivation, the news isn't all bad, or bad at all. The study also discovered several positive outcomes that can actually outweigh the harmful ones. Though these types of employees are motivated by the desire to avoid negative consequences, they are also motivated by the excitement of pursuing emotional rewards. This excitement makes pursuing goals enjoyable and stimulates pleasure and pride that would result from success. An effect of the positive motivation is that it neutralizes the existence of negative motivation.\nSure, it affects people's personal lives to what could be deemed an unhealthy extent, because leisure activities are often seen as a part of life that must be sacrificed to manage work and family demands. However, the way people feel about their work has less to do with whether they're motivated by the preservation of self-esteem but more with the fact that they're simply motivated.", "50": "Many people associate their self-worth with their work. The more successful their career, the better they feel about themselves. Work-related self-esteem is therefore a worthy ideal to pursue with vigor, right? Well, not always. According to recent research, in which psychologists interviewed 370 full-time workers over a period of three weeks, the reality is a little more complicated. And it involves negative as well as positive consequences.\nIt's natural to be drawn towards pleasure and to step away from pain. In the workplace, if that pleasure comes from a triumph which swells our self-respect, people will try to repeat the accomplishment. But repeating that accomplishment is often not realistic, which can lead to severe negative emotional consequences when it doesn't reoccur. This form of motivation is widely regarded as a negative type of motivation. It can hinder other more positive motivation types, such as completing a task purely because it's fulfilling or enjoyable.\nWhat consumes the employee instead is a pressing need to feel mighty and sure of themselves. They then take on only tasks and objectives which serve that ego-driven need. As a result, to avoid feelings of shame and worthlessness associated with failure, they extend themselves to such a degree that there's a subsequent adverse effect on their well-being. This internal pressure to succeed at all costs demands a lot of effort. It depletes their energy, culminating in disproportionate levels of damaging sentiment.\nThose negative emotions mount into heightened anxiety, impacting their ability to make the most of their personal life. Their desire to avoid feeling inferior ends up making them feel inferior when it comes to their diminished capacity for friendship and leisure. They end up dissatisfied both at work and outside of it.\nBut thankfully, for those people compelled almost entirely by this specific form of motivation, the news isn't all bad, or bad at all. The study also discovered several positive outcomes that can actually outweigh the harmful ones. Though these types of employees are motivated by the desire to avoid negative consequences, they are also motivated by the excitement of pursuing emotional rewards. This excitement makes pursuing goals enjoyable and stimulates pleasure and pride that would result from success. An effect of the positive motivation is that it neutralizes the existence of negative motivation.\nSure, it affects people's personal lives to what could be deemed an unhealthy extent, because leisure activities are often seen as a part of life that must be sacrificed to manage work and family demands. However, the way people feel about their work has less to do with whether they're motivated by the preservation of self-esteem but more with the fact that they're simply motivated.", "51": "Degradation of the world's natural resources by humans is rapidly outpacing the planet's ability to absorb the damage, a recent UN environmental study has found. The study concludes that without radical action the level of prosperity that millions of people in the developed world count on will be impossible to maintain or extend to poorer countries.\nWater scarcity is the curse of some of the poorest regions on Earth, leaving developing countries increasingly unable to feed themselves, and causing hardship for millions of people. There appears little prospect of this desperate situation being remedied without radical action being taken. Water resources are under increasing threat from population growth, climate change, rapid urbanization, rising levels of consumption, and the degradation of lands that previously provided a natural replenishment(补充) of water resources.\nThe rate of damage to the natural environment was found to increase globally, despite concerted efforts to persuade government to take measures to improve the condition. \"If current trends continue, and the world fails to improve patterns of production and consumption, then the state of the world's environment will continue to decline,\" warned UN executive director Achim Steiner.\nHe said the tools for improving the environment for millions of people existed in developed countries, but were in danger of not being used.\nThe study found that basic measures to tackle some of the key causes of environmental damage were still not being taken. These included measures to reduce air pollution; to control the damage to marine ecosystems, which can have a huge effect on fish stocks on which hundreds of millions of people depend; and to curb the degradation of land where modern agricultural methods were pursued without regard to the longer-term consequences.\nDespite the recent global agreement on cutting greenhouse gas emissions, global carbon output continues to rise. This will put a long-term strain on the ability of developing economies to feed their own people. Climate change is aggravated by the emissions of greenhouse gases from chemical and natural fertilisers used in agriculture which increased by more than a quarter between 2000 and 2010. Other problem areas identified in the report included glaciers, which provide vital water resources for millions of people, but which are shrinking as the climate warms.\nIn rich countries, these problems have built up over decades and centuries while economic growth was pursued at the expense of the environment. Subsequent efforts to remedy the environment have met with partial success. But in developing countries, the path of future development has more potential to change, which has encouraged international institutions to devise more sustainable growth pathways that are supposed both to alleviate poverty and preserve the environment.", "52": "Degradation of the world's natural resources by humans is rapidly outpacing the planet's ability to absorb the damage, a recent UN environmental study has found. The study concludes that without radical action the level of prosperity that millions of people in the developed world count on will be impossible to maintain or extend to poorer countries.\nWater scarcity is the curse of some of the poorest regions on Earth, leaving developing countries increasingly unable to feed themselves, and causing hardship for millions of people. There appears little prospect of this desperate situation being remedied without radical action being taken. Water resources are under increasing threat from population growth, climate change, rapid urbanization, rising levels of consumption, and the degradation of lands that previously provided a natural replenishment(补充) of water resources.\nThe rate of damage to the natural environment was found to increase globally, despite concerted efforts to persuade government to take measures to improve the condition. \"If current trends continue, and the world fails to improve patterns of production and consumption, then the state of the world's environment will continue to decline,\" warned UN executive director Achim Steiner.\nHe said the tools for improving the environment for millions of people existed in developed countries, but were in danger of not being used.\nThe study found that basic measures to tackle some of the key causes of environmental damage were still not being taken. These included measures to reduce air pollution; to control the damage to marine ecosystems, which can have a huge effect on fish stocks on which hundreds of millions of people depend; and to curb the degradation of land where modern agricultural methods were pursued without regard to the longer-term consequences.\nDespite the recent global agreement on cutting greenhouse gas emissions, global carbon output continues to rise. This will put a long-term strain on the ability of developing economies to feed their own people. Climate change is aggravated by the emissions of greenhouse gases from chemical and natural fertilisers used in agriculture which increased by more than a quarter between 2000 and 2010. Other problem areas identified in the report included glaciers, which provide vital water resources for millions of people, but which are shrinking as the climate warms.\nIn rich countries, these problems have built up over decades and centuries while economic growth was pursued at the expense of the environment. Subsequent efforts to remedy the environment have met with partial success. But in developing countries, the path of future development has more potential to change, which has encouraged international institutions to devise more sustainable growth pathways that are supposed both to alleviate poverty and preserve the environment.", "53": "Degradation of the world's natural resources by humans is rapidly outpacing the planet's ability to absorb the damage, a recent UN environmental study has found. The study concludes that without radical action the level of prosperity that millions of people in the developed world count on will be impossible to maintain or extend to poorer countries.\nWater scarcity is the curse of some of the poorest regions on Earth, leaving developing countries increasingly unable to feed themselves, and causing hardship for millions of people. There appears little prospect of this desperate situation being remedied without radical action being taken. Water resources are under increasing threat from population growth, climate change, rapid urbanization, rising levels of consumption, and the degradation of lands that previously provided a natural replenishment(补充) of water resources.\nThe rate of damage to the natural environment was found to increase globally, despite concerted efforts to persuade government to take measures to improve the condition. \"If current trends continue, and the world fails to improve patterns of production and consumption, then the state of the world's environment will continue to decline,\" warned UN executive director Achim Steiner.\nHe said the tools for improving the environment for millions of people existed in developed countries, but were in danger of not being used.\nThe study found that basic measures to tackle some of the key causes of environmental damage were still not being taken. These included measures to reduce air pollution; to control the damage to marine ecosystems, which can have a huge effect on fish stocks on which hundreds of millions of people depend; and to curb the degradation of land where modern agricultural methods were pursued without regard to the longer-term consequences.\nDespite the recent global agreement on cutting greenhouse gas emissions, global carbon output continues to rise. This will put a long-term strain on the ability of developing economies to feed their own people. Climate change is aggravated by the emissions of greenhouse gases from chemical and natural fertilisers used in agriculture which increased by more than a quarter between 2000 and 2010. Other problem areas identified in the report included glaciers, which provide vital water resources for millions of people, but which are shrinking as the climate warms.\nIn rich countries, these problems have built up over decades and centuries while economic growth was pursued at the expense of the environment. Subsequent efforts to remedy the environment have met with partial success. But in developing countries, the path of future development has more potential to change, which has encouraged international institutions to devise more sustainable growth pathways that are supposed both to alleviate poverty and preserve the environment.", "54": "Degradation of the world's natural resources by humans is rapidly outpacing the planet's ability to absorb the damage, a recent UN environmental study has found. The study concludes that without radical action the level of prosperity that millions of people in the developed world count on will be impossible to maintain or extend to poorer countries.\nWater scarcity is the curse of some of the poorest regions on Earth, leaving developing countries increasingly unable to feed themselves, and causing hardship for millions of people. There appears little prospect of this desperate situation being remedied without radical action being taken. Water resources are under increasing threat from population growth, climate change, rapid urbanization, rising levels of consumption, and the degradation of lands that previously provided a natural replenishment(补充) of water resources.\nThe rate of damage to the natural environment was found to increase globally, despite concerted efforts to persuade government to take measures to improve the condition. \"If current trends continue, and the world fails to improve patterns of production and consumption, then the state of the world's environment will continue to decline,\" warned UN executive director Achim Steiner.\nHe said the tools for improving the environment for millions of people existed in developed countries, but were in danger of not being used.\nThe study found that basic measures to tackle some of the key causes of environmental damage were still not being taken. These included measures to reduce air pollution; to control the damage to marine ecosystems, which can have a huge effect on fish stocks on which hundreds of millions of people depend; and to curb the degradation of land where modern agricultural methods were pursued without regard to the longer-term consequences.\nDespite the recent global agreement on cutting greenhouse gas emissions, global carbon output continues to rise. This will put a long-term strain on the ability of developing economies to feed their own people. Climate change is aggravated by the emissions of greenhouse gases from chemical and natural fertilisers used in agriculture which increased by more than a quarter between 2000 and 2010. Other problem areas identified in the report included glaciers, which provide vital water resources for millions of people, but which are shrinking as the climate warms.\nIn rich countries, these problems have built up over decades and centuries while economic growth was pursued at the expense of the environment. Subsequent efforts to remedy the environment have met with partial success. But in developing countries, the path of future development has more potential to change, which has encouraged international institutions to devise more sustainable growth pathways that are supposed both to alleviate poverty and preserve the environment.", "55": "Degradation of the world's natural resources by humans is rapidly outpacing the planet's ability to absorb the damage, a recent UN environmental study has found. The study concludes that without radical action the level of prosperity that millions of people in the developed world count on will be impossible to maintain or extend to poorer countries.\nWater scarcity is the curse of some of the poorest regions on Earth, leaving developing countries increasingly unable to feed themselves, and causing hardship for millions of people. There appears little prospect of this desperate situation being remedied without radical action being taken. Water resources are under increasing threat from population growth, climate change, rapid urbanization, rising levels of consumption, and the degradation of lands that previously provided a natural replenishment(补充) of water resources.\nThe rate of damage to the natural environment was found to increase globally, despite concerted efforts to persuade government to take measures to improve the condition. \"If current trends continue, and the world fails to improve patterns of production and consumption, then the state of the world's environment will continue to decline,\" warned UN executive director Achim Steiner.\nHe said the tools for improving the environment for millions of people existed in developed countries, but were in danger of not being used.\nThe study found that basic measures to tackle some of the key causes of environmental damage were still not being taken. These included measures to reduce air pollution; to control the damage to marine ecosystems, which can have a huge effect on fish stocks on which hundreds of millions of people depend; and to curb the degradation of land where modern agricultural methods were pursued without regard to the longer-term consequences.\nDespite the recent global agreement on cutting greenhouse gas emissions, global carbon output continues to rise. This will put a long-term strain on the ability of developing economies to feed their own people. Climate change is aggravated by the emissions of greenhouse gases from chemical and natural fertilisers used in agriculture which increased by more than a quarter between 2000 and 2010. Other problem areas identified in the report included glaciers, which provide vital water resources for millions of people, but which are shrinking as the climate warms.\nIn rich countries, these problems have built up over decades and centuries while economic growth was pursued at the expense of the environment. Subsequent efforts to remedy the environment have met with partial success. But in developing countries, the path of future development has more potential to change, which has encouraged international institutions to devise more sustainable growth pathways that are supposed both to alleviate poverty and preserve the environment."}, "questions": [{"id": "2022-12-1-l-1", "type": "listening", "typeZh": "听力", "qno": 1, "stem": "What does the woman say about her dissertation?", "options": ["A) She hasn't started writing it.", "B) She hasn't decided on a topic.", "C) She is proofreading the first draft.", "D) She is working on the references."], "answer": "A", "analysis": "【答案】A （细节题） She hasn't started writing it.\n【定位】W: Oh, I haven't even started writing mine yet, so I'm really worried about finishing by the\nend of next semester.\n女：哦，我连写都还没开始呢，所以我真的很担心能不能在下学期末之前完成。\n【信号】被问者的直接应答。男生先问 How's your dissertation going，女生张口第一句 I haven't\neven started writing mine yet 就是对提问的直接应答，对话题的答案就落在被问者这第一\n反应上。\n【替换】I haven't even started writing mine yet ↔ She hasn't started writing it.\n去掉 even 的同义压缩\n【排除】B) 偷换概念\nShe hasn't decided on a topic. 听着也像『没进展』，但女生说的是还没开始写，topic 在\n后文 I'm still researching the topic 里指『还在查资料』，并非『没定下题目』，属偷换\n概念。\n借用原文：I'm still researching the topic\nC) 张冠李戴\nShe is proofreading the first draft. 里 proofreading the first draft 确在录音中出现，但\n说这话的是男生 I'm proofreading my first draft，不是女生，张冠李戴。\n借用原文：I'm proofreading my first draft\nD) 未提及\nShe is working on the references. 说她在弄参考文献，意味着正文已近完成，与她『还没\n动笔』完全矛盾，录音里也没说她在做文献，属未提及。", "points": ["听力·长对话", "细节题"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-l-2", "type": "listening", "typeZh": "听力", "qno": 2, "stem": "What does the man say about his professor?", "options": ["A) He lent many books to the man for reference.", "B) He offered the man advice on resource hunting", "C) He published a lot in a number of reputable journals.", "D) He told the man to be selective when using e-resources."], "answer": "B", "analysis": "【答案】B （细节题） He offered the man advice on resource hunting\n【定位】M: I started by talking to my professor about where to look for information, and based on\nthat, I found books in the library and a lot of reputable journal articles on the Internet.\n男：我一开始是去找我教授聊该上哪儿找资料，在这个基础上，我在图书馆找到了书，还在\n网上找到很多有声望的期刊文章。\n【信号】经过句里的求助动作。男生回顾自己怎么做研究，关键在 I started by talking to my\nprofessor about where to look for information——他教授给的正是『去哪找资料』的指\n点，这句叙述里藏着教授的作为。\n【替换】talking to my professor about where to look for information ↔\nHe offered the man advice on resource hunting\n把『聊去哪找资料』概括为『给找资料建议』\n【排除】A) 原词陷阱\nHe lent many books to the man for reference. 里 books 确在录音出现，但 I found\nbooks in the library 是男生自己在图书馆找到的书，不是教授借给他的，原词陷阱。\n借用原文：I found books in the library\nC) 原词陷阱\nHe published a lot in a number of reputable journals. 用了原词 reputable journal，但\na lot of reputable journal articles on the Internet 说的是男生在网上找到这些文章来\n读，而非教授在期刊上发表论文，原词陷阱兼无中生有。\n借用原文：a lot of reputable journal articles on the Internet\nD) 未提及\nHe told the man to be selective when using e-resources. 说教授叮嘱『用电子资源要有\n选择』，但录音里教授只指点了去哪找，从未提『要挑着用』，selective 是未提及。", "points": ["听力·长对话", "细节题"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-l-3", "type": "listening", "typeZh": "听力", "qno": 3, "stem": "What does the woman say about her professor?", "options": ["A) He didn't think her dissertation topic viable.", "B) He wasn't interested in her dissertation topic.", "C) He didn't want her to rush through her dissertation.", "D) He wasn't specific about the length of her dissertation."], "answer": "A", "analysis": "【答案】A （细节题） He didn't think her dissertation topic viable.\n【定位】W: And honestly, my professor did warn me at the beginning that I might not be able to find\nenough material.\n女：说实话，我教授一开始就警告过我，我可能找不到足够的材料。\n【信号】引述动词 warn 引出原话。女生用 my professor did warn me at the beginning that I\nmight not be able to find enough material 转述教授当初的警告，引述动词 warn 后面\n那句就是教授的态度，是答案句。\n【替换】warn me at the beginning that I might not be able to find enough material ↔\nHe didn't think her dissertation topic viable.\n『找不到材料』即『选题不可行』\n【排除】B) 张冠李戴\nHe wasn't interested in her dissertation topic. 把 interested 安在教授身上，但录音里 I\nwas so interested in the topic 说有兴趣的是女生自己，教授只是警告找不到料，张冠李戴\n又偷换。\n借用原文：I was so interested in the topic\nC) 未提及\nHe didn't want her to rush through her dissertation. 说教授不想她赶工，但教授只警告\n材料不够，从没说过快慢、赶不赶的事，未提及。\nD) 原词陷阱\nHe wasn't specific about the length of her dissertation. 提到 length，录音里 length\n出现在 my department's minimum length is 70 pages，那是系里的规定，与教授说没说\n清篇幅无关，原词陷阱。\n借用原文：my department's minimum length is 70 pages", "points": ["听力·长对话", "细节题"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-l-4", "type": "listening", "typeZh": "听力", "qno": 4, "stem": "What do we learn the woman will do to complete her dissertation?", "options": ["A) Change her research methodology.", "B) Narrow down her dissertation topic.", "C) Consult her professor more.", "D) Follow the man's advice."], "answer": "D", "analysis": "【答案】D （细节题） Follow the man's advice.\n【定位】W: Broadening the topic is a great idea, I'll start by including folklore from other regions of\nthe country.\n女：把题目扩大是个好主意，我打算先把全国其他地区的民间传说也纳进来。\n【信号】结尾采纳建议的应答。男生上一句建议 You could find more material if you made the\ntopic broader，女生末句 Broadening the topic is a great idea 当即采纳，结尾这句『接\n受建议』就是答案句。\n【替换】Broadening the topic is a great idea ↔ Follow the man's advice.\n采纳男生提议=照他建议办\n【排除】A) 原词陷阱\nChange her research methodology. 沾了男生那句 Maybe the problem is the way\nyou're doing your research，但女生最终决定的是扩大题目，并没说要换研究方法，原词\n陷阱。\n借用原文：Maybe the problem is the way you're doing your research\nB) 与原文相反\nNarrow down her dissertation topic. 与女生的决定正好相反——男生说题目 That's\npretty narrow，建议 made the topic broader，女生要做的是 broaden（扩大）而非\nnarrow（缩小），与原文相反。\n借用原文：That's pretty narrow\nC) 原词陷阱\nConsult her professor more. 里 professor 全程反复出现，诱人选；但女生采纳的是男生\n当下的建议，并未表示要再去多问教授，原词陷阱。\n借用原文：our professors are here to guide us", "points": ["听力·长对话", "细节题"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-l-5", "type": "listening", "typeZh": "听力", "qno": 5, "stem": "What does the woman say about the man in her introduction?", "options": ["A) He has translated 12 books.", "B) He is a well-known nutritionist.", "C) His books sell well worldwide.", "D) His latest book sold a million copies."], "answer": "C", "analysis": "【答案】C （细节题） His books sell well worldwide.\n【定位】That's very modest of you to say, considering that your four books have sold a total of seven\nmillion copies worldwide, and they've been translated into 12 different languages.\n您这么说太谦虚了，毕竟您的四本书在全球总共卖出了七百万册，还被翻译成了 12 种不同\n的语言。\n【信号】主持人介绍嘉宾的成就陈述句。答案信号是主持人介绍环节里铺陈嘉宾业绩的那句 your\nfour books have sold a total of seven million copies worldwide——访谈开场的 \"夸业\n绩\" 句往往就是 introduction 题的答案句。\n【替换】sold a total of seven million copies worldwide ↔ His books sell well worldwide\n\"全球卖出七百万册\" 概括为 \"全球畅销\"\n【排除】A) 原词陷阱\n录音说 translated into 12 different languages(译成 12 种语言)，A 却说 He has\ntranslated 12 books.(翻译了 12 本书)——盗用了原文数字 12，却把对象从 \"语言\" 换成\n\"书\"，且作者是 \"被翻译\" 不是 \"去翻译\"，听到 12 就选必中招。\n借用原文：translated into 12 different languages\nB) 未提及\n录音介绍他是 a respected writer 和写科学的 celebrity authors，从没说他是 a well-\nknown nutritionist.(知名营养师)。营养师是顺着 \"减肥饮食\" 话题脑补出来的，原文未提\n及。\nD) 原词陷阱\n录音是 your four books have sold a total of seven million copies(四本书合计七百万\n册)，D 说 His latest book sold a million copies.(最新一本卖了一百万册)——盗用 \"百万\n册级销量\" 的语感，却把 \"四本合计七百万\" 偷换成 \"单本一百万\"，数字与范围全错。\n借用原文：your four books have sold a total of seven million copies", "points": ["听力·长对话", "细节题"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-l-6", "type": "listening", "typeZh": "听力", "qno": 6, "stem": "What has motivated the man to write his books?", "options": ["A) The desire of Americans to try exotic cuisines.", "B) The demand for information about food safety.", "C) The fact that over half of Americans are overweight.", "D) The fact that science books are difficult to read."], "answer": "C", "analysis": "【答案】C （细节题） The fact that over half of Americans are overweight.\n【定位】Well, people read my books because more than 60% of Americans are overweight, or obese.\n嗯，人们读我的书，是因为超过 60% 的美国人超重，甚至肥胖。\n【信号】因果连接词 because 引出原因。答案信号是显性因果词 because：people read my\nbooks because more than 60% of Americans are overweight，because 后面那句现象\n即为写书/读书的动机。\n【替换】more than 60% of Americans are overweight, or obese ↔\nThe fact that over half of Americans are overweight\n\"超 60%\" 等价于 \"过半\"\n【排除】A) 未提及\nThe desire of Americans to try exotic cuisines.(想尝异国菜)在整段对话里没有任何对\n应，纯属话题跑偏的捏造，与减肥饮食主线无关。\nB) 未提及\nThe demand for information about food safety.(对食品安全信息的需求)听上去与饮食沾\n边，但录音给的动机是 \"超重\"，从未谈 food safety，属顺着话题脑补的未提及项。\nD) 与原文相反\n录音里 \"科学难懂\" 是被作者 make difficult science easy for laymen to understand 克服\n的难点、是卖点，而非写书动机；D 却把 science books are difficult to read. 说成动机，\n盗用了 \"difficult science\" 的字眼却把作用讲反了。\n借用原文：make difficult science easy for laymen to understand", "points": ["听力·长对话", "细节题"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-l-7", "type": "listening", "typeZh": "听力", "qno": 7, "stem": "Who does the man say his last book was mainly written for?", "options": ["A) The general public.", "B) Those who are overweight.", "C) Those who want to lose weight.", "D) The medical community."], "answer": "D", "analysis": "【答案】D （细节题） The medical community.\n【定位】My last book was written primarily for the medical community. But this time, I want to help\nordinary people take control of their weight.\n我上一本书主要是为医学界写的。但这一次，我想帮助普通人掌控自己的体重。\n【信号】限定词 last + 受众句，并与 \"this time\" 对照。答案信号是 My last book was written\nprimarily for the medical community 这句明确的 \"上一本 written for 谁\"，紧接的 But\nthis time 形成 \"上一本 vs 这一本\" 对照，提醒要选 last 对应的那一群。\n【替换】My last book was written primarily for the medical community ↔ The medical community\n受众原词直接对应\n【排除】A) 张冠李戴\nThe general public. 对应的是 this time, I want to help ordinary people——那是 \"这一\n本(新书)\" 的受众。把 this time 的受众安到 last book 头上，正是没分清两本书的张冠李\n戴。\n借用原文：this time, I want to help ordinary people take control of their weight\nB) 原词陷阱\nThose who are overweight. 借了通篇出现的 overweight 一词，但录音从没说哪本书是\n\"为超重者\" 而写；它只是话题词，不是 last book 的受众。\n借用原文：more than 60% of Americans are overweight\nC) 答非所问\nThose who want to lose weight. 贴合全场减肥主题、最顺耳，但录音说 last book 是写\n给 medical community 的；\"想减肥的人\" 从未被点名为某本书的受众，是借主题诱选。", "points": ["听力·长对话", "细节题"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-l-8", "type": "listening", "typeZh": "听力", "qno": 8, "stem": "What does the man recommend people do?", "options": ["A) Switch to a vegetarian diet.", "B) Follow a personalized diet.", "C) Adhere to doctors' advice.", "D) Cut carbohydrate intake."], "answer": "B", "analysis": "【答案】B （细节题） Follow a personalized diet.\n【定位】Briefly, I argue that every person needs to consider their metabolism and eat what suits their\nbody's needs. I don't advocate one single diet.\n简单说，我主张每个人都要考虑自己的新陈代谢，吃适合自己身体需求的东西。我不提倡某\n一种单一的食谱。\n【信号】主张句 I argue + 否定 I don't advocate 立反差。答案信号是主张句 I argue that every\nperson needs to consider their metabolism and eat what suits their body's needs，\n再以 I don't advocate one single diet 否定 \"单一食谱\"——一立一否，强调的正是 \"因人\n而异\"。\n【替换】every person needs to consider their metabolism and eat what suits their body's needs ↔\nFollow a personalized diet\n\"按各自身体需求吃\" 概括为 \"个性化饮食\"\nI don't advocate one single diet ↔ Follow a personalized diet\n\"不主张单一食谱\" 反面印证 \"个性化\"\n【排除】A) 未提及\nSwitch to a vegetarian diet.(改吃素)在对话里没有依据；录音末尾虽提到多吃蔬果，但那\n是补充建议，从没让人 \"改成素食\"，属未提及的绝对化主张。\nC) 原词陷阱\nAdhere to doctors' advice. 借了前文 the medical community 留下的 \"医学\" 印象，但作\n者建议的是按自身代谢来，从没让普通人 \"遵医嘱\"，是盗用医学语感的诱选。\n借用原文：My last book was written primarily for the medical community\nD) 与原文相反\n录音说 Some people should eat more carbohydrates than others(有些人该比别人多吃\n碳水)，是 \"碳水因人而异\"；D 却笼统说 Cut carbohydrate intake.(减少碳水)，盗用\ncarbohydrate 一词，却把 \"看人而定\" 讲成了 \"一律削减\"，方向相反。\n借用原文：Some people should eat more carbohydrates than others", "points": ["听力·长对话", "细节题"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-l-9", "type": "listening", "typeZh": "听力", "qno": 9, "stem": "What did researchers discover about rats placed briefly in a stressful situation?", "options": ["A) The rate of their growth increased dramatically.", "B) The growth of their new brain cells doubled.", "C) They began to show signs of depression.", "D) They began to get irritated and restless."], "answer": "B", "analysis": "【答案】B （细节题） The growth of their new brain cells doubled.\n【定位】Researchers discovered that placing rats in a stressful situation for just a few hours doubled\nthe growth of new brain cells.\n研究者发现，把大鼠置于压力情境中仅仅几个小时，就使其新脑细胞的生长翻了一倍。\n【信号】discovered 后接发现内容。答案句由 Researchers discovered that 引出，研究动词\ndiscovered 后面紧跟的就是题干要的发现，是天然的答案信号；同时 doubled the growth\nof new brain cells 给出明确的量化结果，更确认这就是落点。\n【替换】doubled the growth of new brain cells ↔ The growth of their new brain cells doubled.\n主被动语序调换\n【排除】A) 偷换概念\nA 说 rate of their growth increased dramatically（成长速率剧增），但录音说的是生长\n翻倍（数量翻番），讲的是结果量而非速率；它盗用了原文 growth 一词，却把翻倍偷换成\n速率剧增，答非所问。\n借用原文：doubled the growth of new brain cells\nC) 未提及\nC 说大鼠出现 signs of depression（抑郁迹象），但录音通篇讲的是适度压力的好处，从\n未提大鼠抑郁，属于无中生有。\nD) 未提及\nD 说大鼠变得 irritated and restless（烦躁不安），录音只说短暂压力让脑细胞翻倍、记忆\n变好，没说大鼠情绪烦躁，是凭压力等于负面的常识硬加的，未提及。", "points": ["听力·篇章", "细节题"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-l-10", "type": "listening", "typeZh": "听力", "qno": 10, "stem": "Why do people tend to have clear memories of dangerous situations they have encountered?", "options": ["A) To avoid them in the future.", "B) To warn others against them.", "C) To make good sense of them.", "D) To reflect on their causes."], "answer": "A", "analysis": "【答案】A （细节题） To avoid them in the future.\n【定位】Viewed from a biological perspective, this makes sense, because animals that are better at\nremembering dangerous situations can avoid them in the future.\n从生物学角度看，这是有道理的，因为更善于记住危险情境的动物能在将来躲开它们。\n【信号】because 引出真原因。答案句的核心信号是 because，题干问 Why，录音里紧跟 because\n后的 can avoid them in the future 正是要的原因——因果连词后面就是答案落点。\n【替换】can avoid them in the future ↔ To avoid them in the future.\n几乎原义照搬\n【排除】B) 未提及\nB 说为了 warn others against them（警告别人提防），录音只说记住是为了自己将来躲\n开，从未提及把危险告诉他人，属未提及。\nC) 未提及\nC 说为了 make good sense of them（弄懂它们），录音讲的目的是 avoid（躲开）而非\n理解其含义，方向不符，原文无此说法。\nD) 未提及\nD 说为了 reflect on their causes（反思其成因），录音从没提反思危险的起因，只说记住\n以便将来躲开，是凭常识硬推的目的，未提及。", "points": ["听力·篇章", "细节题"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-l-11", "type": "listening", "typeZh": "听力", "qno": 11, "stem": "What do scientists believe chronic stress can do?", "options": ["A) Produce a surprising healing effect.", "B) Weaken one's immunity in the long run.", "C) Make people more susceptible to illness.", "D) Provide protection against mental illnesses."], "answer": "C", "analysis": "【答案】C （细节题） Make people more susceptible to illness.\n【定位】Scientists concede that chronic stress can make you more prone to illness.\n科学家承认，长期压力会让你更容易生病。\n【信号】concede 后的让步内容。答案句出现题干关键词 chronic stress，并由 Scientists concede\nthat 引出科学家的让步看法；问 chronic 就只认带 chronic 的这句，其后的 make you\nmore prone to illness 即答案。\n【替换】make you more prone to illness ↔ Make people more susceptible to illness.\n近义词替换\n【排除】A) 张冠李戴\nA 说产生 surprising healing effect（惊人疗愈效果），录音里令人意外的好处是说短期压\n力 provide some protection against getting sick，而题干问的是 chronic（长期）；A\n张冠李戴，把短期压力的好处安到了长期压力头上。\n借用原文：short periods of stress can actually provide some protection against getting sick\nB) 与原文相反\nB 说 Weaken one's immunity in the long run（长期削弱免疫力），录音讲免疫只说短期\n压力 increases your immune functioning（增强免疫），从没说长期压力削弱免疫；B 反\n了方向又借用 long run 来唬人。\n借用原文：increases your immune functioning\nD) 偷换概念\nD 说 protection against mental illnesses（防护精神疾病），录音说的是短期压力\nprovide some protection against getting sick（防普通生病），既错把长期当短期，又\n把笼统的生病偷换成 mental illnesses（精神疾病）。\n借用原文：provide some protection against getting sick", "points": ["听力·篇章", "细节题"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-l-12", "type": "listening", "typeZh": "听力", "qno": 12, "stem": "What does the speaker say is a common problem with managers?", "options": ["A) Placing their own interests over their staff's.", "B) Being overwhelmed by their daily routines.", "C) Lacking the ability to relate to their staff.", "D) Spending too much time handling email."], "answer": "D", "analysis": "【答案】D （细节题） Spending too much time handling email.\n【定位】When presented with a choice between the appeal of their inbox and other more important\nactivities, many sacrifice the latter. Daily email demands have a negative impact on their\ngoal progress.\n当要在收件箱的诱惑与其他更重要的事务之间做选择时，许多人牺牲了后者（更重要的\n事）。每天的邮件需求对他们的目标推进产生了负面影响。\n【信号】概括管理者通病的陈述句。这句不是靠某个转折词跳出来，而是全篇反复落到同一点：管理\n者把精力压在邮箱上而牺牲更重要的事。many sacrifice the latter 与 prioritize email\nmanagement over people management 互相印证，共同指向\"花太多时间在邮件上\"这个\n通病。\n【替换】Daily email demands have a negative impact on their goal progress ↔\nSpending too much time handling email\n\"邮件占用精力\"换说成\"花太多时间处理邮件\"\n【排除】A) 偷换概念\n录音说的是管理者把邮件管理置于人员管理之上 prioritize email management over\npeople management，置于上面的是\"邮件\"而非\"自身利益\"；A 把 over...staff 的句式留\n下，却换成 own interests，是偷换。\n借用原文：prioritize email management over people management\nB) 原词陷阱\n录音强调的是被\"邮件\"困住，未说被泛泛的\"日常事务（daily routines）\"压垮；B 借了\nday-to-day 的感觉 day-to-day email，却把焦点从\"邮件\"扩大成\"日常琐事\"，范围被放\n大。\n借用原文：day-to-day email\nC) 过度推断\n录音只说管理者沉迷邮箱、忽视员工 prevents them from dealing with their\nemployees，是\"没空管\"，并未说他们\"缺乏与员工共情的能力（relate to staff）\"；从\"没\n空管\"推到\"没能力\"是多走了一步。\n借用原文：prevents them from dealing with their employees", "points": ["听力·篇章", "细节题"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-l-13", "type": "listening", "typeZh": "听力", "qno": 13, "stem": "What may happen when managers ignore minor problems?", "options": ["A) Their leadership may be challenged.", "B) Their companies may go bankrupt.", "C) Unexpected events may occur.", "D) Major problems may result."], "answer": "D", "analysis": "【答案】D （细节题） Major problems may result.\n【定位】As a result, they ignore the issues that might only be mild problems at first, until\nunfortunately, they inevitably transform into a major problem or crisis by virtue of neglect.\n结果，他们忽视了那些起初可能只是轻微问题的事，直到这些问题不幸地、不可避免地因疏\n忽而演变成重大问题或危机。\n【信号】until 之后才是结果落点。因果信号在 until unfortunately, they inevitably transform\ninto a major problem or crisis：起初只是 mild problems，until 之后才转成 major\nproblem。听这类题不能停在\"小问题\"那半句，落点在 until / transform into 之后的\n结果。\n【替换】transform into a major problem or crisis ↔ Major problems may result\n\"演变成重大问题\"=\"重大问题随之产生\"\n【排除】A) 张冠李戴\n录音前文确实提到 leadership skills 会下降 diminished leadership skills，但那是讲邮件\n焦虑的背景，不是\"忽视小问题\"这一动作的后果；A 把别处出现的 leadership 搬来当本题\n结果，张冠李戴。\n借用原文：diminished leadership skills\nB) 过度推断\n录音最重只说到 major problem or crisis（重大问题或危机），并未说严重到\"公司破产\"；\nB 把\"危机\"夸大为\"破产\"，超出录音程度。\nC) 与原文相反\n录音用 inevitably transform（不可避免地演变）强调这是必然结果，而 C 说\"unexpected\nevents（意外事件）\"，恰与\"不可避免\"相反。\n借用原文：they inevitably transform", "points": ["听力·篇章", "细节题"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-l-14", "type": "listening", "typeZh": "听力", "qno": 14, "stem": "What are leaders expected to do in pursuing their strategic goals?", "options": ["A) Keep an eye on their employees.", "B) Motivate and inspire their team.", "C) Sacrifice some of the immediate goals.", "D) Have greater ambition in overall planning."], "answer": "B", "analysis": "【答案】B （细节题） Motivate and inspire their team.\n【定位】As leaders, they are expected to motivate and inspire their team in pursuit of longer-term\nstrategic goals and also, less ambitiously but more practically, to monitor their daily output, to\nset clear expectations and to give regular feedback.\n作为领导者，他们被期望去激励和鼓舞团队以追求更长远的战略目标，同时，作为志向稍低\n但更务实的一面，去监督日常产出、设定明确预期并给予定期反馈。\n【信号】are expected to + 限定语 in pursuit of strategic goals。信号是 expected to\nmotivate and inspire their team in pursuit of longer-term strategic goals：be\nexpected to 直接给出\"被期望做的事\"，而题干限定\"追求战略目标时\"，正好对应 in\npursuit of...strategic goals 这一半，落点就在 motivate and inspire。\n【替换】motivate and inspire their team in pursuit of longer-term strategic goals ↔\nMotivate and inspire their team\n原句动作原样保留\n【排除】A) 答非所问\n录音里\"监督\"出现在 to monitor their daily output，这属于后半句\"志向稍低、更务实\"的\n日常事务，而非题干所问的\"追求战略目标\"那部分；A 借 monitor 的意思，却挂错了半句。\n借用原文：to monitor their daily output\nC) 原词陷阱\n录音 P4 说的是管理者\"牺牲更重要的事\" many sacrifice the latter，并不是\"牺牲眼前目\n标\"，且那是讲管理者的毛病、不是\"被期望做的事\"；C 把 sacrifice 一词搬来制造熟悉感。\n借用原文：many sacrifice the latter\nD) 过度推断\n录音只说战略目标是 longer-term（更长远）longer-term strategic goals，并未要求领\n导\"在整体规划上更有野心\"；D 把\"长远\"擅自升级成\"更大野心的规划\"。\n借用原文：longer-term strategic goals", "points": ["听力·篇章", "细节题"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-l-15", "type": "listening", "typeZh": "听力", "qno": 15, "stem": "How can a manager best avoid being distracted by email?", "options": ["A) Cultivate self-control.", "B) Filter their email boxes.", "C) Respond only after work.", "D) Check only when necessary."], "answer": "A", "analysis": "【答案】A （细节题） Cultivate self-control.\n【定位】The solution is cultivating self-control which is like a muscle—it can be strengthened or\nimproved over time through exercise.\n解决办法是培养自控力，它就像一块肌肉——可以通过锻炼随时间不断增强或提升。\n【信号】The solution is 给总方案。信号是 The solution is cultivating self-control：The\nsolution is 直接抛出总的解决办法。题干带 best，要的正是这条根本方案，而其后的\nmaking space in your diary、setting a timer 等都只是它名下的\"具体小做法\"，不是\n总解。\n【替换】The solution is cultivating self-control ↔ Cultivate self-control\n总方案原样对应\n【排除】B) 原词陷阱\n录音确实念到 check, filter and respond to emails 里有 filter，但那是描述邮件耗费精\n力，不是给的解决建议；filter 一词制造了熟悉感，却答非\"best 的总办法\"。\n借用原文：check, filter and respond to emails\nC) 未提及\n录音的具体建议是\"在日程里划出专门查邮件的时段\" making space in your diary for the\nonly periods during which you'll be checking emails，并没有说\"只在下班后回复\"；C\n是凭常识臆造的做法。\nD) 答非所问\n录音建议是\"划定专门时段查\"与\"设定时器\" setting a timer for yourself so you don't\nbecome distracted，更接近 D 的味道，但 D 仍只是 self-control 名下的具体操作；题干\n带 best，要的是总方案 A 而非这条小招。\n借用原文：making space in your diary for the only periods during which you'll be checking emails", "points": ["听力·篇章", "细节题"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-l-16", "type": "listening", "typeZh": "听力", "qno": 16, "stem": "What does the speaker say a team of marketing professors has studied?", "options": ["A) The key to increasing healthy food supply.", "B) The best way to improve marketing research.", "C) The impact of advertisements on consumption.", "D) The importance of the appearance of food."], "answer": "D", "analysis": "【答案】D （细节题） The importance of the appearance of food.\n【定位】Well, a team of marketing professors has studied the importance of the visual aspect of food\nand how that influences food choices.\n嗯，一组营销学教授研究了食物视觉方面的重要性，以及它如何影响食物选择。\n【信号】题干原词 studied 在原文直接出现。录音 a team of marketing professors has studied\nthe importance of the visual aspect of food 与题干同用 studied，是对研究对象的直接\n交代，定位信号明确，无需转折或推断。\n【替换】the importance of the visual aspect of food ↔ The importance of the appearance of food.\nvisual aspect 同义改写为 appearance\n【排除】A) 原词陷阱\n选项把录音多次提到的 healthy 拼成 increasing healthy food supply，但录音研究的是外\n观对选择的影响，从未谈增加健康食品的供给量，属听到 healthy 就想选的原词陷阱。\n借用原文：promote healthy food choices\nB) 原词陷阱\n选项借用录音里的 marketing 拼成 improve marketing research，但讲者说的是营销学者\n拿来研究外观，而非研究如何改进市场调研本身，属答非所问。\n借用原文：a team of marketing professors\nC) 原词陷阱\n录音确实在 seeing an appealing photograph of a hamburger in an advertisement 提\n到广告，但那是用来举例说明外观如何起作用，不是这组学者研究的对象；选项把举例细节\n当成研究主题，属原词陷阱。\n借用原文：an appealing photograph of a hamburger in an advertisement", "points": ["听力·讲座", "细节题"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-l-17", "type": "listening", "typeZh": "听力", "qno": 17, "stem": "How have medical professionals tried to fight obesity?", "options": ["A) By focusing on the nutrients in different foods.", "B) By emphasizing the diversity of food.", "C) By stressing pleasing aesthetics of food.", "D) By winning the support of marketing professors."], "answer": "A", "analysis": "【答案】A （细节题） By focusing on the nutrients in different foods.\n【定位】medical professionals have tried to fight the obesity epidemic by focusing on the nutrients\nfound in different foods, emphasizing things like carbohydrate, fat, sugar and calorie content.\n医学专家曾试图通过关注不同食物中的营养成分来对抗肥胖流行病，强调诸如碳水化合物、\n脂肪、糖和卡路里含量之类的东西。\n【信号】主体词 medical professionals 领出做法句。录音 medical professionals have tried to\nfight the obesity epidemic by focusing on the nutrients 主体与题干完全一致，by\nfocusing on 直接给出做法，是该主体名下的答案句信号。\n【替换】by focusing on the nutrients found in different foods ↔\nBy focusing on the nutrients in different foods.\n几乎原句对应仅省略 found\n【排除】B) 未提及\n选项 By emphasizing the diversity of food. 的 diversity 在录音里从未出现，医学专家强\n调的是营养成分而非食物多样性，属无中生有。\nC) 张冠李戴\n强调美感 By stressing pleasing aesthetics of food. 确是录音里的做法，但那是营销学者\n的主张，不是医学专家的做法；选项把营销学者的招安到医学专家头上，属张冠李戴。\n借用原文：the combination of pleasing aesthetics\nD) 原词陷阱\n选项 By winning the support of marketing professors. 借用录音里的 marketing\nprofessors，但录音从没说医学专家去争取营销教授的支持，二者只是讲座中并列对比的两\n方，属原词陷阱。\n借用原文：a team of marketing professors", "points": ["听力·讲座", "细节题"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-l-18", "type": "listening", "typeZh": "听力", "qno": 18, "stem": "What can other companies learn from the example of the carrot promotion campaign?", "options": ["A) They can attract customers with the healthy qualities of their products.", "B) They can boost sales of healthy foods by making them visually appealing.", "C) They can turn to marketing professors for advice.", "D) They can rely on advertising for sales promotion."], "answer": "B", "analysis": "【答案】B （推断题） They can boost sales of healthy foods by making them visually appealing.\n【定位】The researchers believe that other companies could bolster sales of healthy foods with similar\nads, depicting their products as attractive and a source of pleasure.\n研究者认为，其他公司可以用类似的广告来提升健康食品的销量，把它们的产品描绘得有吸\n引力、是一种愉悦的来源。\n【信号】结尾外推句 could+similar 给出启示。录音结尾 other companies could bolster sales of\nhealthy foods with similar ads 用 could 与 similar 把胡萝卜案例外推到其他公司，正是\n题干所问的启示落点。\n【替换】bolster sales of healthy foods with similar ads, depicting their products as attractive ↔\nThey can boost sales of healthy foods by making them visually appealing.\nbolster=boost、attractive=visually appealing\n【排除】A) 与原文相反\n选项 They can attract customers with the healthy qualities of their products. 借用录音\ndidn't emphasize the carrots' healthy qualities 的原词，但录音明说该案例恰恰没强调健\n康属性，选项把否定说成肯定，属与原文相反。\n借用原文：The campaign didn't emphasize the carrots' healthy qualities\nC) 原词陷阱\n选项 They can turn to marketing professors for advice. 借用录音里的 marketing\nprofessors，但讲者说的是公司可用类似广告，从没说让公司去求助营销教授，属原词陷\n阱。\n借用原文：a team of marketing professors\nD) 偷换概念\n选项 They can rely on advertising for sales promotion. 借用录音的 ads，但录音强调的\n是靠把产品拍得有吸引力、令人愉悦的广告，而非泛泛依赖广告；选项丢掉视觉吸引这一关\n键限定，属偷换概念。\n借用原文：bolster sales of healthy foods with similar ads, depicting their products as attractive and\na source of pleasure", "points": ["听力·讲座", "推断题"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-l-19", "type": "listening", "typeZh": "听力", "qno": 19, "stem": "What does the speaker say about the cleaning products industry in recent years?", "options": ["A) It has witnessed a spectacular surge in demand.", "B) It has met much criticism from environmentalists.", "C) It has seen more small businesses offering environment-friendly products.", "D) It has experienced increasingly fierce competition among global companies."], "answer": "C", "analysis": "【答案】C （细节题） It has seen more small businesses offering environment-friendly products.\n【定位】In recent years, however, many countries have witnessed a surge in the number of small\nbusinesses and companies offering more environment-friendly cleaning products, and they're\ndoing good business too.\n然而近年来，许多国家见证了提供更环保清洁用品的小企业和公司数量激增，而且它们的生\n意还相当不错。\n【信号】时间标志 in recent years + 转折 however。In recent years, however 同时给出题干要\n的时间窗和一个转折信号——however 把话锋从前句\"大公司主导\"转向\"小企业崛起\"，转折\n之后才是答案落点。\n【替换】a surge in the number of small businesses and companies offering more environment-friendly\ncleaning products\n↔ more small businesses offering environment-friendly products\na surge in the number of = more 的同义概括\n【排除】A) 原词陷阱\n录音确实念了 surge，但原文是 a surge in the number of small businesses（企业数量激\n增），选项 a spectacular surge in demand 把它偷换成\"需求激增\"，听到 surge 就选会中\n招。\n借用原文：a surge in the number of small businesses and companies\nB) 未提及\n选项 much criticism from environmentalists 在录音里找不到任何对应——原文讲的是环\n保产品走红、生意红火，从无\"被批评\"之说，属凭空捏造。\nD) 原词陷阱\n录音第2段确有 large global companies，选项 fierce competition among global\ncompanies 借这个词造出\"全球公司竞争加剧\"，可原文只说大公司\"主导\"行业，没说它们之\n间竞争更激烈。\n借用原文：dominated by large global companies", "points": ["听力·讲座", "细节题"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-l-20", "type": "listening", "typeZh": "听力", "qno": 20, "stem": "Why are newly developed cleaning products selling well?", "options": ["A) Consumers now know much more about technology.", "B) Their mass production has sharply reduced the price", "C) Consumers tend to favor all that is novel.", "D) Their quality has been greatly improved."], "answer": "A", "analysis": "【答案】A （细节题） Consumers now know much more about technology.\n【定位】The third reason is people's awareness of and knowledge about technology has never been\ngreater. In the past, people might have been skeptical of a new product claimed to be able to\nachieve amazing cleaning results, but they now have faith in technology's ability to do what\nwas once thought impossible.\n第三个原因是，人们对技术的认知和了解从未像现在这样深。过去人们可能会怀疑一款号称\n能达到惊人清洁效果的新产品，但如今他们相信技术有能力做到曾被认为不可能的事。\n【信号】明示标志 The third reason + 对应题干\"new products\"。The third reason is people's\nawareness of and knowledge about technology has never been greater 用 The third\nreason 直接挂出一条理由；题干问的是 newly developed products，对应的正是这条\"人\n们更懂技术、因而信任新产品\"的原因。\n【替换】people's awareness of and knowledge about technology has never been greater ↔\nConsumers now know much more about technology\nknowledge…never been greater = know much more 的同义改写\n【排除】B) 未提及\n选项 mass production has sharply reduced the price 听上去顺理成章，但录音讲好卖的\n原因是环保意识、安全、懂技术，从头到尾没提\"量产降价\"，是用生活常识替代原文。\nC) 过度推断\n选项 favor all that is novel（偏爱一切新奇）看似贴近\"新产品\"，但录音说的是人们 have\nfaith in technology（信任技术能力），不是\"凡新必爱\"，把\"信任技术\"推成\"盲目追新\"推\n过了头。\n借用原文：they now have faith in technology's ability to do what was once thought impossible\nD) 偷换概念\n选项 quality has been greatly improved 录音并未提及——原文讲的是消费者对技术\n的\"认知与信任\"，而非产品\"质量本身\"提高了，二者不能混为一谈。", "points": ["听力·讲座", "细节题"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-l-21", "type": "listening", "typeZh": "听力", "qno": 21, "stem": "What are some customers doing to help promote non-traditional cleaning products?", "options": ["A) Purchasing only this kind of products for home cleaning.", "B) Writing positive comments about them on social media.", "C) Demonstrating on TV how effective these products are.", "D) Telling one another about their incomparable virtues."], "answer": "B", "analysis": "【答案】B （细节题） Writing positive comments about them on social media.\n【定位】Then, in many cases, customers are doing the marketing for these products by leaving threads\nof comments on social media, praising their virtues.\n然后，很多情况下，是顾客在为这些产品做营销——他们在社交媒体上留下一串串评论，称\n赞产品的优点。\n【信号】主语对应 customers + 动作 doing the marketing。customers are doing the\nmarketing for these products 的主语正是题干的 customers、目的正是 help promote\n（做营销=帮推广），后面 by leaving… 直接交代了具体做法，是答案句。\n【替换】leaving threads of comments on social media, praising their virtues ↔\nWriting positive comments about them on social media\nleaving…comments, praising = writing positive comments 的同义改写\n【排除】A) 未提及\n选项 Purchasing only this kind of products 里的 only（只买这一种）录音没有任何依据\n——原文讲顾客帮做营销、写评论，从没说他们\"只\"用这类产品。\nC) 原词陷阱\n录音第4段提过 TV（advertised on TV）、第5段提过 TV shows，选项 Demonstrating\non TV 借这些 TV 造\"上电视演示\"，可原文恰恰说这类产品没在电视宣传、且\"上电视演\n示\"是节目而非顾客所为，听到 TV 就选会中招。\n借用原文：people don't see these products in shops, or advertised on TV or in the press\nD) 原词陷阱\n选项 Telling one another about their incomparable virtues 用了录音的 virtues，但原文\n顾客是\"在社交媒体写评论\"称赞，而非 Telling one another（互相口头转告）；盗了对的\n词、错在渠道。\n借用原文：leaving threads of comments on social media, praising their virtues", "points": ["听力·讲座", "细节题"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-l-22", "type": "listening", "typeZh": "听力", "qno": 22, "stem": "What problem might be caused by the growing piles of coins in fountains?", "options": ["A) Increasing cleaners' workload.", "B) Blocking the fountains' works.", "C) Breaking a time-honored ritual.", "D) Polluting the fountains' water."], "answer": "B", "analysis": "【答案】B （细节题） Blocking the fountains' works.\n【定位】Otherwise, the growing piles of pennies, quarters and euros could clog up the\nfountains' works.\n否则，越堆越多的便士、25 美分和欧元硬币可能会堵塞喷泉的运作机件。\n【信号】Otherwise 引出假设后果。信号是 Otherwise（否则）——它引出\"如果钱不被运走会怎\n样\"的假设性后果，正对题干问的\"会造成什么问题\"，紧跟其后的 could clog up the\nfountains' works 就是答案句的核心。\n【替换】clog up the fountains' works ↔ Blocking the fountains' works\nclog up = Blocking 同义替换\n【排除】A) 原词陷阱\n选项 Increasing cleaners' workload 里的 cleaners 在后文确实反复出现（喷泉由 staff 清\n理），但录音从没说\"硬币堆积会加重清洁工负担\"，是借后文的\"清洁\"话题诱你听到\ncleaners 就选。\n借用原文：They are cleaned by the parks' staff every few weeks.\nC) 原词陷阱\n选项 Breaking a time-honored ritual 直接搬了录音第一句的 time-honored ritual，但那\n句是说\"投币许愿是个老传统\"，是引入话题，根本不是在讲\"硬币堆积造成的问题\"——典型\n的把开头原词拿来骗。\n借用原文：Throwing spare change into a fountain is a time-honored ritual\nD) 未提及\n选项 Polluting the fountains' water 听起来\"硬币泡水里好像会污染\"很合常识，但录音通\n篇没提水质污染，是用生活常识替文本作答的典型坑。", "points": ["听力·讲座", "细节题"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-l-23", "type": "listening", "typeZh": "听力", "qno": 23, "stem": "What does the speaker say about the coins collected from New York City's park fountains?", "options": ["A) They are occasionally retrieved by curious tourists.", "B) They are regularly donated to charity organizations.", "C) They are mostly used for the fountains' maintenance.", "D) They are usually used as wages for fountain cleaners."], "answer": "C", "analysis": "【答案】C （细节题） They are mostly used for the fountains' maintenance.\n【定位】But most of the coins have already been removed by entrepreneurial New Yorkers and there is\nnot a significant amount left to be collected.\n但大部分硬币已经被有生意头脑的纽约人捞走了，剩下能被收走的已所剩无几。\n【信号】转折 But 后才是真意。信号是 But——前半句说\"市政人员每几周清理一次\"是表面信息，转\n折 But 之后的 most of the coins have already been removed by entrepreneurial New\nYorkers 才是录音真正想强调的实情，这正是答案落点。\n【替换】go towards the fountains' maintenance itself ↔ used for the fountains' maintenance\ngo towards=used for 同指用途\n【排除】A) 张冠李戴\n选项 occasionally retrieved by curious tourists 看似对上\"硬币被人提前取走\"，但录音说\n取走硬币的是 entrepreneurial New Yorkers（有生意头脑的纽约人），不是 curious\ntourists（好奇游客）——把取走者的身份偷换了，属张冠李戴。\n借用原文：most of the coins have already been removed by entrepreneurial New Yorkers\nB) 张冠李戴\n选项 donated to charity organizations 里的 charity 录音确有（罗马的钱办惠民超市、迪\n士尼捐寄养儿童），但那是罗马和迪士尼喷泉的事，不是本题问的纽约公园喷泉——张冠李\n戴。\n借用原文：Tens of thousands of dollars in coins removed from wishing wells, fountains and ponds\nin Florida's Walt Disney World are donated each year to support foster children\nD) 未提及\n选项 used as wages for fountain cleaners 里 cleaners / staff 录音确有（喷泉由公园\nstaff 清理），但录音从没说硬币被\"当作清洁工的工资\"，是借\"清洁\"话题拼出的无中生有。\n借用原文：They are cleaned by the parks' staff every few weeks.", "points": ["听力·讲座", "细节题"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-l-24", "type": "listening", "typeZh": "听力", "qno": 24, "stem": "What do we learn about the money collected from Rome's Trevi Fountain?", "options": ["A) It is invested in a series of businesses.", "B) It is used exclusively for its maintenance.", "C) It is used to run a supermarket for the needy.", "D) It is estimated to be about $40,000 a month."], "answer": "C", "analysis": "【答案】C （细节题） It is used to run a supermarket for the needy.\n【定位】Most of the money collected each night goes towards running a supermarket for the needy.\n每晚收上来的钱，大部分用于运营一家面向困难群体的超市。\n【信号】goes towards 点明用途。信号是表用途的 goes towards（用于……）——它直接交代这\n笔钱的去向，紧跟其后的 running a supermarket for the needy 就是答案。听到 goes\ntowards 这类\"用于\"的短语就锁定其后内容。\n【替换】running a supermarket for the needy ↔ run a supermarket for the needy\nrunning→run 仅词形微调\n【排除】A) 原词陷阱\n选项 invested in a series of businesses 里 business(es) 一词录音确有（serious\nbusiness 指\"收钱是件正经事\"），但那是形容\"这事很严肃\"，根本不是说钱拿去\"投资做生\n意\"——盗用 business 一词制造误会。\n借用原文：collecting that cash is serious business\nB) 张冠李戴\n选项 used exclusively for its maintenance 描述的\"专门用于喷泉维护\"是录音里纽约公园\n喷泉和 Bryant Park 喷泉的处置，不是罗马许愿池的，张冠李戴；且 exclusively（专门、\n唯一）程度过死，罗马的钱是\"大部分\"办超市。\n借用原文：which puts the cash collected by cleaners towards the fountain's own maintenance\nD) 与原文相反\n选项 about $40,000 a month 把数字改了：录音说的是 as much as $4,000 in loose\nchange from around the world each day（每天约 4000 美元），选项改成\"每月 4\n万\"——金额和时间单位都被动了手脚，是典型数字陷阱。\n借用原文：getting as much as $4,000 in loose change from around the world each day", "points": ["听力·讲座", "细节题"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-l-25", "type": "listening", "typeZh": "听力", "qno": 25, "stem": "What does the speaker say about Thomas Morgan?", "options": ["A) He was arrested for stealing money from four fountain cleaners.", "B) He was sentenced to 34 years' imprisonment.", "C) He collected rare coins from around the world.", "D) He stole a lot of money from a fountain with a magnetic stick."], "answer": "D", "analysis": "【答案】D （细节题） He stole a lot of money from a fountain with a magnetic stick.\n【定位】Authorities finally caught one notorious thief named Thomas Morgan and banned him\nfrom the fountain after he fished out thousands of dollars in change over 34 years using a\nmagnetic stick.\n当局最终抓获一名臭名昭著、名叫 Thomas Morgan 的小偷，并禁止他靠近喷泉——此前\n他用一根磁棒在 34 年间钓走了数千美元的零钱。\n【信号】人名 + 其后动作链。信号是人名 named Thomas Morgan 一出现就锁定本句，重点在它\n后面的动作链 fished out thousands of dollars in change over 34 years using a\nmagnetic stick——\"用磁棒钓走数千美元\"就是答案核心。\n【替换】fished out thousands of dollars in change ↔ stole a lot of money from a fountain\nfished out=stole 概括偷取\nusing a magnetic stick ↔ with a magnetic stick\nusing=with 同指工具\n【排除】A) 张冠李戴\n选项 arrested for stealing money from four fountain cleaners 里的 four fountain\ncleaners 录音确有，但那是 2005 年警方抓的\"四名监守自盗的清洁工\"，是另一桩案子，跟\nThomas Morgan 无关——把别人的事安到他头上，还把\"四名清洁工\"从\"被抓的人\"偷换\n成\"被偷的对象\"。\n借用原文：police arrested four fountain cleaners after they were spotted slipping coins into their\nown pockets\nB) 原词陷阱\n选项 sentenced to 34 years' imprisonment 盗用录音的数字 34 years，但录音说的是他\nover 34 years 间一直作案，结果只是被 banned from the fountain（禁入喷泉），并没\n有\"判刑 34 年\"——把\"作案时长\"偷换成\"刑期\"。\n借用原文：banned him from the fountain after he fished out thousands of dollars in change over\n34 years\nC) 原词陷阱\n选项 collected rare coins from around the world 里 from around the world 录音确有\n（罗马许愿池收来自世界各地的零钱），但那是说硬币来源广，不是说 Morgan\"收藏稀有\n硬币\"——他是偷钱不是藏币，纯属拼凑别处原词造的无中生有。\n借用原文：as much as $4,000 in loose change from around the world each day", "points": ["听力·讲座", "细节题"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-c-26", "type": "cloze", "typeZh": "选词填空", "qno": 26, "stem": "", "options": ["A) access", "B) apparent", "C) barely", "D) dedication", "E) escorted", "F) froze", "G) incredible", "H) indignant", "I) network", "J) overriding", "K) peacefully", "L) presumably", "M) stifled", "N) struck", "O) terrifying"], "answer": "F", "analysis": "【答案】F) froze\n动词\n【词性槽】主语 We all 后缺谓语动词，需一般过去时\n【依据】听到『我有三把枪』后所有人本能呆住\n上文 I have three guns and I want to use them. 是极端威胁，紧接 We all 的反应只能是\n吓得僵住——freeze 正是英语里表达『因恐惧而瞬间不动』的高频动词，与下文 I was\ndizzy with fear. 形成连贯的恐惧反应链。\n【竞争词】E) escorted 及物动词，缺宾语\nescort 意为『护送某人』，必须带宾语，而句子是 We all __(26)__. 后面直接句号，无宾语；且\n『我们护送了』也对不上听到威胁后的第一反应。\nM) stifled 及物且语义不符\nstifle 通常作及物动词（压抑哭声/笑声），后面缺宾语；语义上『我们都压抑了』也无对象，语\n境不通。\nN) struck 强搭配指向第 31 题\nstrike 在此语境里更常以 crisis struck（危机突然发生）这一固定搭配出现，后文 crisis __(31)__\nagain 才是它的归宿；用在 26 空只能解作『打击/击中』，缺宾语也不成句。", "points": ["选词填空", "词性判断·主语 We all 后缺谓语动词，需一般"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-c-27", "type": "cloze", "typeZh": "选词填空", "qno": 27, "stem": "", "options": ["A) access", "B) apparent", "C) barely", "D) dedication", "E) escorted", "F) froze", "G) incredible", "H) indignant", "I) network", "J) overriding", "K) peacefully", "L) presumably", "M) stifled", "N) struck", "O) terrifying"], "answer": "A", "analysis": "【答案】A) access\n名词\n【词性槽】介词 without 后接名词\n【依据】access to 是固定搭配，意为『使用权』\nhave/without access to + 物 是英语里表达『（无法）获得/使用某物』的标准搭配。原句\nwithout access to her medications 即『无法获得自己的药物』，与精神分裂症患者发病\n的语境完全契合：因为没药才会发作、闯进课堂。\n【竞争词】D) dedication 语义荒诞\ndedication 指『奉献、专注』，dedication to her medications 字面是『对药物的奉献』，对\n精神患者而言荒诞；语义与上下文医疗背景脱节。\nI) network 搭配指向第 34 题\nnetwork of people / network of homeless 是更经典的搭配，将在第 34 空发挥作用；用在 27\n空 network to her medications 不成习语，搭配生硬。", "points": ["选词填空", "词性判断·介词 without 后接名词"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-c-28", "type": "cloze", "typeZh": "选词填空", "qno": 28, "stem": "", "options": ["A) access", "B) apparent", "C) barely", "D) dedication", "E) escorted", "F) froze", "G) incredible", "H) indignant", "I) network", "J) overriding", "K) peacefully", "L) presumably", "M) stifled", "N) struck", "O) terrifying"], "answer": "E", "analysis": "【答案】E) escorted\n动词\n【词性槽】并列连词 and 后接同形态过去分词\n【依据】escorted away 表『被护送/押送离开』\nescort 常与 in/out/away 搭配，表示有专人带某人离开。原文 wrestled out and\nescorted away, then put in a hospital for observation，先是被拽出去、再被护送走、然\n后送医观察——动作链条流畅自然。\n【竞争词】M) stifled 搭配与语义都不对\nstifled away 不是英语固定搭配；stifle 表『压抑哭声/欲望』，与『从课堂带走精神患者』这一\n物理动作毫不相干。", "points": ["选词填空", "词性判断·并列连词 and 后接同形态过去分词"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-c-29", "type": "cloze", "typeZh": "选词填空", "qno": 29, "stem": "", "options": ["A) access", "B) apparent", "C) barely", "D) dedication", "E) escorted", "F) froze", "G) incredible", "H) indignant", "I) network", "J) overriding", "K) peacefully", "L) presumably", "M) stifled", "N) struck", "O) terrifying"], "answer": "K", "analysis": "【答案】K) peacefully\n副词\n【词性槽】修饰动词 passed，需副词\n【依据】与『despite + I was rattled』形成让步对比\n原句 despite the fact that the rest of our days on campus passed __(29)__, I was\nrattled. 用 despite 引出让步：表面上的日子平静，与内心仍受惊形成反差。peacefully\n（平静地）正好与 rattled（心神不宁）构成『外平静、内不安』的对照。\n【竞争词】C) barely 语义反向，破坏让步逻辑\nbarely 意为『几乎不』，『日子几乎没过去』不成话；且与 despite 之后『虽然…平稳，但我仍\n受惊』的逻辑反向。\nL) presumably 推测语气与亲历叙述冲突\npresumably 表『大概、想必』，用于推测；作者亲身在校园，对自己后续的日子是亲历不是推\n测，语气不匹配。", "points": ["选词填空", "词性判断·修饰动词 passed，需副词"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-c-30", "type": "cloze", "typeZh": "选词填空", "qno": 30, "stem": "", "options": ["A) access", "B) apparent", "C) barely", "D) dedication", "E) escorted", "F) froze", "G) incredible", "H) indignant", "I) network", "J) overriding", "K) peacefully", "L) presumably", "M) stifled", "N) struck", "O) terrifying"], "answer": "G", "analysis": "【答案】G) incredible\n形容词\n【词性槽】介词 at 与名词 risk 之间需形容词\n【依据】at incredible risk 强调难以置信的高风险\nincredible 在这里取『大到难以置信』的语义。前文叙述了课堂枪击威胁，作者由此得出\nwe always live at __(30)__ risk 的结论——『生活在难以置信的高风险里』，与全文的极端\n恐惧场景吻合，且与下段又一桩街头事件互证。\n【竞争词】H) indignant 对象错配\nindignant 修饰人或情绪，an indignant risk 不成习惯搭配，语法上虽通但语义荒诞。\nJ) overriding 色彩偏向中性『首要』\noverriding risk 偏向 commercial/legal 等正式语体里『首要风险』，多用于风险评估；与本句\n日常生活的弥散性恐惧的语感不符，更不如 incredible 突出『程度令人震惊』。\n【易错】最具迷惑性的错误词是 J) —— overriding risk 像高级搭配但语体错位。考生背过\noverriding priority/concern 这类搭配，会自然延伸出 overriding risk，且词性也对、句\n法也通。防坑：本文是抒情散文，谈的是『日常生活里弥散的恐惧』，需要程度词\n（incredible），不是商务正式语体里的『首要风险』。判断不准时回到全文情绪基调——\n能与 I was dizzy with fear. 共振的，才是答案。", "points": ["选词填空", "词性判断·介词 at 与名词 risk 之间需形容"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-c-31", "type": "cloze", "typeZh": "选词填空", "qno": 31, "stem": "", "options": ["A) access", "B) apparent", "C) barely", "D) dedication", "E) escorted", "F) froze", "G) incredible", "H) indignant", "I) network", "J) overriding", "K) peacefully", "L) presumably", "M) stifled", "N) struck", "O) terrifying"], "answer": "N", "analysis": "【答案】N) struck\n动词\n【词性槽】主语 crisis 后缺谓语动词\n【依据】crisis struck again 是地道高频搭配\nstrike 作不及物动词时常表示『（灾难/危机/事故）突然降临』，crisis/disaster/tragedy\nstruck 是固定句式。本段开头 A few months later, crisis __(31)__ again. 正是用这一句承\n接上一段课堂事件，引出新的危机——结构上与 Each part of the episode was as\nhaunting as it was __(35)__. 所暗示的反复灾祸呼应。\n【竞争词】E) escorted 及物且语义反向\nescort 必须带人作宾语；且 crisis escorted 字面是『危机护送』，毫无意义。\nM) stifled 主语错位\nstifle 是『压抑、扼制』，主语通常是人或机构（压抑某种东西），crisis stifled 反过来了，且\nstifle 也需要宾语，本句缺。", "points": ["选词填空", "词性判断·主语 crisis 后缺谓语动词"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-c-32", "type": "cloze", "typeZh": "选词填空", "qno": 32, "stem": "", "options": ["A) access", "B) apparent", "C) barely", "D) dedication", "E) escorted", "F) froze", "G) incredible", "H) indignant", "I) network", "J) overriding", "K) peacefully", "L) presumably", "M) stifled", "N) struck", "O) terrifying"], "answer": "B", "analysis": "【答案】B) apparent\n形容词\n【词性槽】no 与名词 reason 之间需形容词修饰\n【依据】for no apparent reason 是固定搭配\nfor no apparent reason 意为『没有明显的理由』，是英语里描述行为突兀、动机不明的常\n用表达。陌生女子毫无来由抱走孩子，正符合此意——上文 Swiftly and for no __(32)__\nreason 用 Swiftly 强调动作之突兀，apparent 与之呼应。\n【竞争词】H) indignant 感情色彩错位\nindignant 形容『义愤填膺的』，用于描述人或情绪，而非 reason；an indignant reason 不成\n搭配，逻辑上女子也并非出于义愤。\nJ) overriding 搭配相反\noverriding reason 意为『压倒一切的理由』，是『有强烈理由』；与本句 no（没有）连用语义\n自相矛盾——无『压倒一切』的理由是把强调有理由的词放到了否定语境，明显别扭。", "points": ["选词填空", "词性判断·no 与名词 reason 之间需形容词"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-c-33", "type": "cloze", "typeZh": "选词填空", "qno": 33, "stem": "", "options": ["A) access", "B) apparent", "C) barely", "D) dedication", "E) escorted", "F) froze", "G) incredible", "H) indignant", "I) network", "J) overriding", "K) peacefully", "L) presumably", "M) stifled", "N) struck", "O) terrifying"], "answer": "C", "analysis": "【答案】C) barely\n副词\n【词性槽】主谓之间修饰动词 cried\n【依据】事情发生太快太懵，孩子几乎没来得及哭\n上文 It was so fast and confusing 已经为此空铺垫——动作迅猛、孩子来不及反应。\nbarely cried 即『几乎没哭出声』，与『fast and confusing』因果连贯：还没反应过来，\n父亲就追上抢回了孩子。\n【竞争词】L) presumably 推测语气与亲历叙述冲突\npresumably 表『大概』，是写作者对未亲见之事的推测；但作者一家亲历整段，包括孩子的反\n应，无须推测，语气错位。\n【易错】最具迷惑性的错误词是 L) —— presumably 看似谨慎但叙述视角不对。副词组只剩 C/L 两\n个，presumably cried 也能勉强解为『大概哭了』，似乎留有余地；但本段是作者一家亲\n历，连孩子叫了别人孩子的名字这种细节都记得，没必要用『大概』。防坑：副词二选一时\n回看叙述视角——亲历用具体程度词（barely），未亲见才用推测词（presumably）。", "points": ["选词填空", "词性判断·主谓之间修饰动词 cried"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-c-34", "type": "cloze", "typeZh": "选词填空", "qno": 34, "stem": "", "options": ["A) access", "B) apparent", "C) barely", "D) dedication", "E) escorted", "F) froze", "G) incredible", "H) indignant", "I) network", "J) overriding", "K) peacefully", "L) presumably", "M) stifled", "N) struck", "O) terrifying"], "answer": "I", "analysis": "【答案】I) network\n名词\n【词性槽】冠词 A 与 of 短语之间的主语位置\n【依据】a network of homeless people 表『流浪者之间的人际网』\nnetwork of + 人群 指『某群体的人际网络』，与定语从句 who generally know the\nother homeless in the area 完美呼应——彼此互相认识的群体正是『一张网』。\n【竞争词】D) dedication 搭配与单复数都不对\ndedication of homeless people 不构成英语习惯搭配；且 dedication 表抽象品质，与定语从\n句『相互认识』的群体属性无关。", "points": ["选词填空", "词性判断·冠词 A 与 of 短语之间的主语位置"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-c-35", "type": "cloze", "typeZh": "选词填空", "qno": 35, "stem": "", "options": ["A) access", "B) apparent", "C) barely", "D) dedication", "E) escorted", "F) froze", "G) incredible", "H) indignant", "I) network", "J) overriding", "K) peacefully", "L) presumably", "M) stifled", "N) struck", "O) terrifying"], "answer": "O", "analysis": "【答案】O) terrifying\n形容词\n【词性槽】as…as 比较结构后接形容词\n【依据】与 haunting 同色调、共同收束恐怖基调\nhaunting 意为『萦绕心头、挥之不去的（恐惧）』，与 terrifying（令人恐惧的）感情色彩\n一致——孩子被陌生人抱走这一段经历，既挥之不去又骇人。这个收尾与第二段 I couldn't\nshake the sense that in this country we always live at __(30)__ risk. 的恐惧基调一脉相\n承，是全文情感的回扣。\n【竞争词】G) incredible 词义模糊，色彩不齐\nincredible 表『难以置信』，可褒可贬；与 haunting 的负面色调虽不冲突但不够对位，而\nincredible 已在 30 题作为更精准的『难以估量的风险』所需。\nH) indignant 对象错配\nindignant 是『义愤的』，形容人或情绪，不修饰 episode（事件）。\nJ) overriding 语义不搭\noverriding 是『压倒一切的、最重要的』，an overriding episode 不成英语；与 haunting 也\n不构成同色调对应。", "points": ["选词填空", "词性判断·as…as 比较结构后接形容词"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-m-36", "type": "match", "typeZh": "信息匹配", "qno": 36, "stem": "Wardian regards the various extraordinary challenges as a test of his physical endurance", "options": null, "answer": "E", "analysis": "【答案】E 段（弱锚点）\n【锚点】把各种非凡挑战当作身体耐力的测试\n【定位】I love diverse and unique challenges, he said. I'm definitely interested in seeing what I can\nhandle and what my body can accept. That drives me.\n「我热爱多样而独特的挑战，」他说，「我非常想看看自己能扛多少、身体能接受到什么程\n度。这正是驱动我前进的东西。」\n【改写】the various extraordinary challenges ↔ diverse and unique challenges\n形容词同义词替换\na test of his physical endurance ↔ seeing what I can handle and what my body can accept\n动词短语被概括为抽象名词（名词化）\n【辨邻】 L L段的核心是if you're not seeking things out that are challenging and difficult for\nyou, then you're not growing——是「成长论」而非「身体耐力测试论」，话题相邻\n但命题方向不同。\nI want to always keep doing things that are exciting, adventurous, different and most importantly,\nprobably things I'm not the best at\nK K段焦点在Once he decides to do something, he just works at it until he does it\n——这是「决心-执行力」的评价，与「身体耐力测试」无关。\nOnce he decides to do something, he just works at it until he does it", "points": ["信息匹配·同义替换"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-m-37", "type": "match", "typeZh": "信息匹配", "qno": 37, "stem": "Wardian hopes his participation in the seven-day marathon series will contribute to a worthy cause.", "options": null, "answer": "I", "analysis": "【答案】I 段（弱锚点）\n【锚点】希望以七日赛参与为公益事业出力\n【定位】Wardian, too, hopes his involvement will give him a platform to promote a cause. He recently\nbecame an ambassador for the United Nations Women's HeForShe initiative to fight\ninequalities faced by women and girls worldwide.\nWardian同样希望，自己的这次参赛能给他一个平台来推动某项事业。他不久前成为联合国\nHeForShe运动的形象大使，旨在反抗全球女性和女孩面临的不平等。\n【改写】his participation in the seven-day marathon series ↔ his involvement\n概括上位（具体到抽象）\nwill contribute to a worthy cause ↔ will give him a platform to promote a cause\n动作同义替换+评价性形容词补足\n【辨邻】 L L段焦点是I hope maybe people see what I do, and say, Okay, I want to do\nsomething different or try something new——是个体激励层面，与陈述句要的\n「contribute to a worthy cause」（推动公益事业）不在同一命题上。\nI hope maybe people see what I do", "points": ["信息匹配·同义替换"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-m-38", "type": "match", "typeZh": "信息匹配", "qno": 38, "stem": "Wardian is going to join over thirty other runners in a week-long marathon series.", "options": null, "answer": "D", "analysis": "【答案】D 段（强锚点）\n【锚点】与三十多名跑者一起加入为期一周的马拉松系列赛\n【定位】He will line up Monday in Antarctica for the first leg of the World Marathon Challenge—\njoining 32 other adventure seekers on an unusual journey where participants travel through\ndifferent time zones and climates to run seven marathons on seven continents in seven days.\n他将于周一在南极站上世界马拉松挑战赛的第一段起点——与另外32位冒险者一同踏上这趟\n非凡之旅：参赛者们穿越不同时区与气候，在七天里跑完七大洲的七场马拉松。\n【改写】over thirty other runners ↔ 32 other adventure seekers\n数字落入范围+下位词替换\na week-long marathon series ↔ seven marathons on seven continents in seven days\n时间+赛事被压缩成抽象表述\n【辨邻】 H H段强调阵容more elite，没说人数；陈述句要的是「数量超过30人」的具体事实，匹\n配点必须落在D段。\nThis year's challenge will feature a far more elite field, which includes Ryan Hall, America's fastest\nmarathon runner", "points": ["信息匹配·同义替换"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-m-39", "type": "match", "typeZh": "信息匹配", "qno": 39, "stem": "Over-exertion in extreme cold can lower one's body temperature to a dangerous point.", "options": null, "answer": "A", "analysis": "【答案】A 段（强锚点）\n【锚点】极寒下用力过猛会把体温降到危险点\n【定位】Too much effort and he'd begin to sweat, which, he was told, would only increase the risk\nof hypothermia.\n用力过猛他就会开始出汗，而别人告诉他，那只会增加体温过低的风险。\n【改写】Over-exertion in extreme cold ↔ Too much effort and he'd begin to sweat\n动作描述对应：用力过猛=Over-exertion\ncan lower one's body temperature to a dangerous point ↔\nwould only increase the risk of hypothermia\n专有术语的白话定义改写\n【辨邻】 B B段焦点在天气数据和外部风险（北极熊），没有把「过度用力」与「体温下降」挂钩\n——而陈述句问的正是这条机理。\nAt the 2014 North Pole Marathon, the temperature dipped to minus-22 degrees F, with a wind chill\nthat made it feel even colder\nC C段关注的是Wardian通过比赛战胜his aversion to the cold，是心理层面，与陈述句\n的生理机理（用力—出汗—失温）不在同一维度。\nThe race for Wardian, however, was less about the result than overcoming his aversion to the cold", "points": ["信息匹配·同义替换"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-m-40", "type": "match", "typeZh": "信息匹配", "qno": 40, "stem": "Wardian was very much impressed by a race director's sense of adventure.", "options": null, "answer": "F", "analysis": "【答案】F 段（强锚点）\n【锚点】某位赛事总监的冒险气质打动了Wardian\n【定位】Something about the way Richard Donovan carried himself appealed to Wardian. Perhaps it\nwas the sense of adventure Donovan displayed when they first met at the 2010 50K\nChampionships in Galway, Ireland, where Donovan was the race director.\nRichard Donovan的某种气质打动了Wardian。也许就是2010年爱尔兰Galway的50K锦标\n赛上、Donovan作为赛事总监出场时所展现的那种冒险精神。\n【改写】was very much impressed by ↔\nSomething about the way Richard Donovan carried himself appealed to Wardian\n动词同义替换：impressed by≈appealed to\na race director's sense of adventure ↔\nthe sense of adventure Donovan displayed when they first met at the 2010 50K Championships\nin Galway, Ireland, where Donovan was the race director\n名词搭配原样复现\n【辨邻】 K K段焦点是妹妹对其性格的评价，跟陈述句要的「赛事总监的冒险气质打动了\nWardian」完全不在一条线上。\nOnce he decides to do something, he just works at it until he does it", "points": ["信息匹配·同义替换"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-m-41", "type": "match", "typeZh": "信息匹配", "qno": 41, "stem": "Once Wardian sets his mind on something, he is determined to make it happen.", "options": null, "answer": "K", "analysis": "【答案】K 段（强锚点）\n【锚点】一旦下决心做某事，就一定让它成真\n【定位】Once he decides to do something, he just works at it until he does it, Michael's younger sister,\nMariele, said. Once he decides to do it, it's usually something that's going to happen.\n「一旦他决定做某件事，他就会一直坚持到做成为止。」Michael的妹妹Mariele说，「一旦\n他决定要做，那件事通常就会成真。」\n【改写】Once Wardian sets his mind on something ↔ Once he decides to do something\n习语同义替换\nhe is determined to make it happen ↔ he just works at it until he does it\n决心+持续动作=必达结果\n【辨邻】 L L段焦点是if you're not seeking things out that are challenging and difficult for\nyou, then you're not growing——是成长哲学，与陈述句要的「下定决心就一定做\n成」是不同命题。\nI want to always keep doing things that are exciting, adventurous, different and most importantly,\nprobably things I'm not the best at\nE E段强调diverse and unique challenges与what my body can accept，是挑战类型\n与身体测试，并未提出「决心即必达」。\nI'm definitely interested in seeing what I can handle and what my body can accept. That drives me", "points": ["信息匹配·同义替换"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-m-42", "type": "match", "typeZh": "信息匹配", "qno": 42, "stem": "One top American marathoner quit his running career because of his physical condition.", "options": null, "answer": "H", "analysis": "【答案】H 段（强锚点）\n【锚点】某位美国顶尖马拉松选手因身体状况退出跑步生涯\n【定位】Despite his proven track record, Hall said he has no time goals and that he still suffers from\nthe same fatigue issues that forced him to leave the professional ranks in 2015.\n尽管成绩斐然，Hall表示自己不设时间目标，并且仍在承受当年迫使他在2015年退出职业赛\n场的那种疲劳问题。\n【改写】One top American marathoner ↔ Ryan Hall, America's fastest marathon runner\n形容词同义集合：top等于fastest\nquit his running career ↔ forced him to leave the professional ranks in 2015\n被动结果与主动动作互换\nbecause of his physical condition ↔ fatigue issues\n具体症状被概括为身体状况\n【辨邻】 I I段的焦点是「完赛即回报」与「借赛公益」的不同动机，没有任何「美国顶尖马拉松\n选手退役」的命题。\nsimply finishing will be its own reward", "points": ["信息匹配·同义替换"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-m-43", "type": "match", "typeZh": "信息匹配", "qno": 43, "stem": "To many of the week-long marathon participants, completing the race will be a success in itself.", "options": null, "answer": "I", "analysis": "【答案】I 段（弱锚点）\n【锚点】对许多周赛参与者而言，完赛本身就是成功\n【定位】To others on the trip, simply finishing will be its own reward.\n对这趟旅程里的其他人来说，仅仅完赛本身就是一种回报。\n【改写】To many of the week-long marathon participants ↔ To others on the trip\n范围限定的同义替换\ncompleting the race will be a success in itself ↔ simply finishing will be its own reward\n完赛即回报=完赛即成功\n【辨邻】 E 陈述句的主体是「许多周赛参与者」（非Wardian一人）；E段只讲Wardian自己。同\n时E段从未把「完赛」等同于「成功」，命题维度也不同。\nI'm definitely interested in seeing what I can handle and what my body can accept. That drives me\nG G段焦点在getting comfortable being uncomfortable——讲完赛过程中要承受不\n适，而非「完赛本身就是成功」。\nThe key to a race like this is getting comfortable being uncomfortable", "points": ["信息匹配·同义替换"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-m-44", "type": "match", "typeZh": "信息匹配", "qno": 44, "stem": "For Wardian, the marathon in the Arctic was more about how to triumph over the extreme cold.", "options": null, "answer": "C", "analysis": "【答案】C 段（强锚点）\n【锚点】北极那场马拉松对Wardian来说重点在战胜极寒\n【定位】The race for Wardian, however, was less about the result than overcoming his aversion to\nthe cold.\n然而对Wardian来说，这场比赛重点不在成绩，而在战胜自己对寒冷的厌恶。\n【改写】was more about how to triumph over the extreme cold ↔\nwas less about the result than overcoming his aversion to the cold\n比较结构等值替换+动词同义\nthe marathon in the Arctic ↔ The race\n代词性回指被还原为具体赛事\n【辨邻】 A A段是开篇白描+科普机理，未对「赛事的意义」做评价；陈述句要的「赛事意义=战\n胜冷」恰恰只在C段被显式提出。\nToo much effort and he'd begin to sweat, which, he was told, would only increase the risk\nof hypothermia\nB B段焦点在外部环境（温度、风寒、北极熊），不涉Wardian的赛事意义；陈述句的\nhow to triumph over the extreme cold需要主体（Wardian）和对抗动作，B段\n没有。\nAt the 2014 North Pole Marathon, the temperature dipped to minus-22 degrees F", "points": ["信息匹配·同义替换"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-m-45", "type": "match", "typeZh": "信息匹配", "qno": 45, "stem": "To participate in the seven-day marathon series, Wardian had to raise a lot of money and have his wife's support.", "options": null, "answer": "G", "analysis": "【答案】G 段（强锚点）\n【锚点】为参赛Wardian需要筹大笔钱并征得妻子支持\n【定位】Wardian started saving for the trip in 2014, connecting with sponsors and getting approval\nfrom his wife, Jennifer, before committing.\nWardian从2014年起为这趟旅程攒钱、联系赞助商，并在正式报名前征得了妻子Jennifer的\n同意。\n【改写】had to raise a lot of money ↔ started saving for the trip in 2014, connecting with sponsors\n具体动作被概括为抽象动作\nhave his wife's support ↔ getting approval from his wife, Jennifer\napproval等于support的同义概括\n【辨邻】 D D段焦点在「他将参赛+32位同行者」的事实，没有raise a lot of money/wife's\nsupport等备赛准备信息。\nHe will line up Monday in Antarctica for the first leg of the World Marathon Challenge", "points": ["信息匹配·同义替换"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-r-46", "type": "reading", "typeZh": "仔细阅读", "qno": 46, "stem": "What does the author say about the pursuit of work-related self-esteem?", "options": ["A) It may result in negative motivation.", "B) It contributes to one's accomplishments.", "C) It can increase one's vigor as one keeps trying.", "D) It costs too much emotionally and psychologically."], "answer": "A", "analysis": "【答案】A （细节题）\n【判型】What does the author say about the pursuit of work-related self-esteem 直接问作者\n对某话题的陈述，没有 infer/imply，需要回到原文找到该话题的明确表态句。\n【拆句】题干主干 What does the author say about... 是 wh- 疑问句，about 后接介宾 the\npursuit of work-related self-esteem，结构平铺直叙，无陷阱。\n【定位】Work-related self-esteem is therefore a worthy ideal to pursue with vigor, right? Well, not\nalways. According to recent research, in which psychologists interviewed 370 full-time\nworkers over a period of three weeks, the reality is a little more complicated. And it involves\nnegative as well as positive consequences.\n于是工作型自尊就是一个值得全力追求的理想，对吗？嗯，并非总是如此。根据一项让心理\n学家在三周内访谈 370 名全职员工的近期研究，现实要更复杂一些。它既牵涉正面后果，也\n牵涉负面后果。\n【选项】A) ✓ 正确\ninvolves negative as well as positive consequences ↔ It may result in negative motivation\n预判的负面后果在 negative motivation 中被精确收口为研究真正定义的负面后果类型\n——动机层面的负面，故锁定 A。\nB) 与原文相反\nIt contributes to one's accomplishments 把 a worthy ideal to pursue with vigor 当\n成作者真实观点，但作者立刻用 not always 否定了这种乐观说法。\nC) 偷换概念\nIt can increase one's vigor as one keeps trying 把原文中描述追求方式的 with vigor\n改造成追求会增加 vigor，混淆 vigor 作方式状语与作宾语的角色。\nD) 过度推断\nIt costs too much emotionally and psychologically 给出 too much 的程度判断，\n但首段仅说 involves negative as well as positive consequences，并未将代价定性为\n过高。", "points": ["仔细阅读", "细节题"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-r-47", "type": "reading", "typeZh": "仔细阅读", "qno": 47, "stem": "What do employees tend to do in pursuing work-related self-esteem?", "options": ["A) Take on tasks well beyond their actual capabilities.", "B) Strive to succeed at the expense of their well-being.", "C) Resort to all means regardless of the consequences.", "D) Exaggerate their sense of shame and worthlessness."], "answer": "B", "analysis": "【答案】B （细节题）\n【判型】What do employees tend to do 是对客观行为的提问，不要求推断，回原文找直接描述行\n为的句子即可。\n【拆句】题干为 wh- 疑问句，主干 What do employees tend to do，in pursuing work-related\nself-esteem 是介词短语作伴随状语，限定行为发生的语境，无难句。\n【定位】As a result, to avoid feelings of shame and worthlessness associated with failure, they extend\nthemselves to such a degree that there's a subsequent adverse effect on their well-being.\n结果，为了躲开与失败相连的羞耻感和无价值感，他们把自己拉伸到这种程度，以至于随之\n而来的是对其身心健康的不利影响。\n【选项】A) 过度推断\nTake on tasks well beyond their actual capabilities 把 to such a degree that\nthere's a subsequent adverse effect on their well-being 改写为超出实际能力，但原\n文只说付出过度，没说任务超出能力。\nB) ✓ 正确\nthey extend themselves to such a degree that there's a subsequent adverse effect on their well-\nbeing\n↔ Strive to succeed at the expense of their well-being\n预判中的拼命与损害自身两成分被 Strive to succeed 和 at the expense of their well-\nbeing 一一收拢，故锁定 B。\nC) 与原文相反\nResort to all means regardless of the consequences 说他们不顾后果，但原文 to\navoid feelings of shame and worthlessness associated with failure 恰恰说他们极其\n在意后果。\nD) 与原文相反\nExaggerate their sense of shame and worthlessness 把 to avoid feelings of\nshame and worthlessness 改成夸大羞耻感，正话反说。", "points": ["仔细阅读", "细节题"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-r-48", "type": "reading", "typeZh": "仔细阅读", "qno": 48, "stem": "What do we learn about people over-concerned with work-related self-esteem?", "options": ["A) They may often feel inferior to their colleagues.", "B) They cannot enjoy their personal life to the full.", "C) They are never satisfied with their achievements.", "D) They have their own view of friendship and leisure."], "answer": "B", "analysis": "【答案】B （细节题）\n【判型】What do we learn about people over-concerned with work-related self-esteem 询问\n对某类人群的认识，要求回原文找作者对这类人的直接论断。\n【拆句】题干主干 What do we learn about people，过去分词短语 over-concerned with work-\nrelated self-esteem 作 people 的后置定语，限定具体人群，结构清晰。\n【定位】Those negative emotions mount into heightened anxiety, impacting their ability to make the\nmost of their personal life. Their desire to avoid feeling inferior ends up making them feel\ninferior when it comes to their diminished capacity for friendship and leisure.\n那些负面情绪累积成加剧的焦虑，影响他们充分享受个人生活的能力。他们想要避免自卑的\n渴望最终反而让他们在自己对友谊与闲暇的削弱能力面前感到自卑。\n【选项】A) 偷换概念\nThey may often feel inferior to their colleagues 把原文 feel inferior 的对照对象改\n成 colleagues，但原文比较对象是 diminished capacity for friendship and leisure，\n与同事无关。\nB) ✓ 正确\nimpacting their ability to make the most of their personal life ↔\nThey cannot enjoy their personal life to the full\n预判中的个人生活质量被削弱被 cannot enjoy their personal life to the full 完整收\n拢，故锁定 B。\nC) 过度推断\nThey are never satisfied with their achievements 用 never 加 with their\nachievements 描述成就维度的不满，但原文说的是 dissatisfied both at work and\noutside of it，且未升级到 never 的极端否定。\nD) 无中生有\nThey have their own view of friendship and leisure 借 friendship and leisure 词面\n做诱饵，但原文只说他们对友谊与闲暇的能力削弱，从未说他们持独到看法。", "points": ["仔细阅读", "细节题"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-r-49", "type": "reading", "typeZh": "仔细阅读", "qno": 49, "stem": "What is the good news we learn from the recent research?", "options": ["A) The pursuit of goals may turn out to be enjoyable and pleasant.", "B) The emotional rewards from goal pursuit are worth the pains taken.", "C) The negative consequences of goal pursuit can mostly be avoided.", "D) The goal of swelling self-esteem can be achieved if one keeps trying."], "answer": "A", "analysis": "【答案】A （细节题）\n【判型】What is the good news we learn from the recent research 询问原文里明示的正面发\n现，属客观转述，不需推断。\n【拆句】题干主干 What is the good news，we learn from the recent research 是省略关系代词\n的定语从句修饰 news，平铺直叙，无陷阱。\n【定位】Though these types of employees are motivated by the desire to avoid negative consequences,\nthey are also motivated by the excitement of pursuing emotional rewards. This excitement\nmakes pursuing goals enjoyable and stimulates pleasure and pride that would result\nfrom success.\n尽管这些员工受到躲避负面后果的渴望驱使，他们同时也受到追求情感奖赏所带来的兴奋的\n驱使。这种兴奋让追求目标变得令人享受，并激发出本会因成功而产生的愉悦与自豪。\n【选项】A) ✓ 正确\nThis excitement makes pursuing goals enjoyable and stimulates pleasure and pride ↔\nThe pursuit of goals may turn out to be enjoyable and pleasant\n预判中的追求带来享受被 enjoyable and pleasant 完整收拢，故锁定 A。\nB) 无中生有\nThe emotional rewards from goal pursuit are worth the pains taken 引入代价对\n价值的权衡关系，但原文 An effect of the positive motivation is that it neutralizes\nthe existence of negative motivation 只说正面动机中和负面动机，未做代价值得的\n判断。\nC) 过度推断\nThe negative consequences of goal pursuit can mostly be avoided 把 neutralizes\nthe existence of negative motivation 升级为多数可避免，但 neutralize 是抵消、不\n是避免，且原文未说大多数。\nD) 与原文相反\nThe goal of swelling self-esteem can be achieved if one keeps trying 与 repeating\nthat accomplishment is often not realistic 直接冲突；原文明说重复成就并不现实。", "points": ["仔细阅读", "细节题"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-r-50", "type": "reading", "typeZh": "仔细阅读", "qno": 50, "stem": "What can we infer from the last paragraph?", "options": ["A) Workers have to make sacrifices to preserve self-esteem.", "B) Self-esteem swells when workers are strongly motivated.", "C) Pursuit of goals affects people's personal lives to an unhealthy extent.", "D) People feel positive about their work as long as they are motivated."], "answer": "D", "analysis": "【答案】D （推断题）\n【判型】What can we infer from the last paragraph 明示 infer，定位段已锁尾段，要求基于尾段\n明示信息做一步推断。\n【拆句】题干主干 What can we infer，from the last paragraph 是介词短语作状语指出推断的依\n据来源，结构简单。\n【定位】However, the way people feel about their work has less to do with whether they're motivated\nby the preservation of self-esteem but more with the fact that they're simply motivated.\n然而，人们对工作的感受真正取决于的，与其说是他们是否被维护自尊的渴望所驱动，不如\n说是他们到底有没有被驱动这件事本身。\n【选项】A) 偷换概念\nWorkers have to make sacrifices to preserve self-esteem 把 leisure activities are\noften seen as a part of life that must be sacrificed to manage work and family\ndemands 中牺牲闲暇的目的改成 preserve self-esteem，目的错位。\nB) 与原文相反\nSelf-esteem swells when workers are strongly motivated 把因果说成动机强则自尊\n膨胀，但原文 has less to do with whether they're motivated by the preservation\nof self-esteem 反而弱化了自尊在因果链里的地位。\nC) 以偏概全\nPursuit of goals affects people's personal lives to an unhealthy extent 把 Sure, it\naffects people's personal lives to what could be deemed an unhealthy extent 这\n一让步分句当作尾段主结论，但 However 之后才是作者真正立场。\nD) ✓ 正确\nthe way people feel about their work has less to do with whether they're motivated by the\npreservation of self-esteem but more with the fact that they're simply motivated\n↔ People feel positive about their work as long as they are motivated\n预判中的有动机即正向感受被 as long as they are motivated 完整收拢，且 positive\n与文章正向 good news 区段的态度一致，故锁定 D。", "points": ["仔细阅读", "推断题"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-r-51", "type": "reading", "typeZh": "仔细阅读", "qno": 51, "stem": "What is the major finding of the UN environmental study?", "options": ["A) Human activity has rendered Mother Earth almost uninhabitable.", "B) Humans are doing more damage to the earth than it can cope with.", "C) Environmental problems have considerably weakened human prosperity.", "D) Environmental damage is more serious in developed countries these days."], "answer": "B", "analysis": "【答案】B （主旨题）\n【判型】题干 What is the major finding of the UN environmental study? 问的是研究的\"主要发\n现\"，对应全文的中心结论，而非局部细节。\n【拆句】What is the major finding of the UN environmental study? 是典型 wh-疑问句，主干\nWhat is the major finding，of 短语修饰 finding，无从句、无否定，结构平铺直叙，无\n陷阱。\n【选项】A) 无中生有\nMother Earth almost uninhabitable 说地球\"几乎不宜居住\"，原文只说破坏速度超过\n吸收能力，并未提到地球已濒临不宜居住的程度。\nB) ✓ 正确\nDegradation of the world's natural resources by humans is rapidly outpacing the planet's ability\nto absorb the damage\n↔ Humans are doing more damage to the earth than it can cope with\n预判\"破坏速度超过地球承受力\"在 Humans are doing more damage to the earth\nthan it can cope with 中以 more...than it can cope with 完整复现，是定位句的标准\n同义替换。\nC) 偷换概念\n原文意思是\"破坏超过吸收能力会使富国当前繁荣不可维持\"——是\"环境破坏会损害\n繁荣\"的预言；Environmental problems have considerably weakened human\nprosperity 改成\"环境问题已经显著削弱了人类繁荣\"，把未来的预警偷换成已发生的\n事实。\nD) 无中生有\nEnvironmental damage is more serious in developed countries these days 断言发\n达国家环境破坏更严重，原文从未做\"发达国家 vs 发展中国家谁更严重\"的横向比较，是\n无中生有的比较。", "points": ["仔细阅读", "主旨题"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-r-52", "type": "reading", "typeZh": "仔细阅读", "qno": 52, "stem": "What is said about water scarcity in some of the poorest regions?", "options": ["A) It is getting so serious that there is little hope of solution.", "B) It largely accounts for their slow economic development.", "C) It can hardly be relieved if no drastic measures are taken.", "D) It is primarily caused by the acceleration of climate change."], "answer": "C", "analysis": "【答案】C （细节题）\n【判型】题干 What is said about water scarcity in some of the poorest regions? 形式 \"What is\nsaid about X\"，问的是文中对 X 的具体陈述，是典型细节题。\n【拆句】What is said about water scarcity in some of the poorest regions? 被动语态，主干\nWhat is said，about 介词短语带出讨论对象，in 短语限定范围；结构清楚、无陷阱。\n【定位】There appears little prospect of this desperate situation being remedied without radical action\nbeing taken.\n如果不采取激进行动，这种绝望的状况几乎没有得到改善的前景。\n【选项】A) 过度推断\n原文是\"不激进行动则无望\"——前提是\"如果不采取\"，there is little hope of solution\n把条件去掉、直接断言\"几乎无解\"，把有条件的判断推为无条件结论，过度推断。\nB) 张冠李戴\n原文只说水资源短缺让发展中国家 increasingly unable to feed themselves, and\ncausing hardship for millions of people，关心的是粮食与民生；It largely accounts\nfor their slow economic development 转到\"经济发展缓慢\"上，原文未做此因果\n归因。\nC) ✓ 正确\nThere appears little prospect of this desperate situation being remedied without radical action\nbeing taken\n↔ It can hardly be relieved if no drastic measures are taken\n预判\"无激进行动→几乎无望解决\"在 It can hardly be relieved if no drastic measures\nare taken 中以 hardly + if no...are taken 完整复刻，是定位句的标准同义重写。\nD) 以偏概全\n原文罗列了 population growth, climate change, rapid urbanization, rising levels of\nconsumption, and the degradation of lands 五个并列威胁因素；It is primarily\ncaused by the acceleration of climate change 单挑\"气候加剧\"为主因，原文从未做此\n排序。", "points": ["仔细阅读", "细节题"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-r-53", "type": "reading", "typeZh": "仔细阅读", "qno": 53, "stem": "What does Achim Steiner say about the environmental condition?", "options": ["A) It will deteriorate worldwide.", "B) It is attracting global attention.", "C) It is being slowly remedied globally.", "D) It will shrink the world's population."], "answer": "A", "analysis": "【答案】A （细节题）\n【判型】题干 What does Achim Steiner say about the environmental condition? 问具体人物对\n具体话题的具体陈述，属于事实细节，不是推断或主旨。\n【拆句】What does Achim Steiner say about the environmental condition? 主动语态特殊疑问\n句，主干 What does Achim Steiner say，about 短语带出陈述对象，无从句无否定，结构\n透明。\n【定位】If current trends continue, and the world fails to improve patterns of production and\nconsumption, then the state of the world's environment will continue to decline.\n如果当前趋势继续下去，世界又无法改善生产与消费模式，那么全球环境状况将持续恶化。\n【选项】A) ✓ 正确\nthe state of the world's environment will continue to decline ↔ It will deteriorate worldwide\n预判\"环境将持续恶化\"在 It will deteriorate worldwide 中以 will deteriorate 保留 will\n未来时态，worldwide 保留全球范围，整句结构紧贴定位句。\nB) 无中生有\nIt is attracting global attention 说环境正吸引全球关注，原文 Steiner 引语只谈\"将继\n续恶化\"，未提全球对它的关注度。\nC) 与原文相反\nIt is being slowly remedied globally 说环境正在被缓慢修复，与原文 the rate of\ndamage to the natural environment was found to increase globally 及 Steiner 引\n语\"将继续恶化\"完全相反。\nD) 无中生有\nIt will shrink the world's population 说环境状况会缩减世界人口，原文 Steiner 引语\n只字未提人口收缩。", "points": ["仔细阅读", "细节题"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-r-54", "type": "reading", "typeZh": "仔细阅读", "qno": 54, "stem": "What is the dilemma developing countries face?", "options": ["A) They cannot modernise farming without causing land degradation.", "B) They cannot promote industrialisation without polluting waterways.", "C) They cannot boost crop yields without causing greenhouse gas emissions.", "D) They cannot catch up with rich countries without sacrificing the environment."], "answer": "C", "analysis": "【答案】C （细节题）\n【判型】题干 What is the dilemma developing countries face? 问的是文中明确描述的具体两\n难，是文中实有陈述的细节，不是推理。\n【拆句】What is the dilemma developing countries face? 主干 What is the dilemma，后接省\n略关系代词的定语从句 (which/that) developing countries face 修饰 dilemma；基础薄\n弱考生易把 face 误解为名词\"面孔\"，须留意它在此是及物动词\"面对\"。\n【定位】This will put a long-term strain on the ability of developing economies to feed their own\npeople. Climate change is aggravated by the emissions of greenhouse gases from chemical\nand natural fertilisers used in agriculture which increased by more than a quarter between\n2000 and 2010.\n这（碳排放上升）将长期压制发展中经济体养活本国人口的能力。气候变化又被农业中化肥\n（化学与天然）所排放的温室气体所加剧——这类排放在 2000 到 2010 年间增长了超过四\n分之一。\n【选项】A) 张冠李戴\ncannot modernise farming without causing land degradation 是\"现代化农业导致\n土地退化\"，原文第 5 段才提 curb the degradation of land where modern\nagricultural methods were pursued，但与本题第 6 段的\"养人 vs 温室气体\"两难是两\n个不同话题。\nB) 无中生有\ncannot promote industrialisation without polluting waterways 说\"工业化必然污染\n水道\"，原文未谈发展中国家工业化的两难，也未谈水道污染。\nC) ✓ 正确\nThis will put a long-term strain on the ability of developing economies to feed their own people\n↔ boost crop yields\nClimate change is aggravated by the emissions of greenhouse gases from chemical and natural\nfertilisers used in agriculture\n↔ causing greenhouse gas emissions\n预判\"养人靠提产、提产致排放\"在 They cannot boost crop yields without causing\ngreenhouse gas emissions 中以 cannot...without... 双重否定形式把目的与代价绑成\n两难，与原文两面对应。\nD) 偷换概念\ncannot catch up with rich countries without sacrificing the environment 说\"追赶\n富国必牺牲环境\"，这是 P7 谈\"富国曾以环境换增长\"的引申、且原文 P7 的态度是发展\n中国家\"有潜力改变路径\"——选项把 P7 的论点反向化，又错放进本题两难。", "points": ["仔细阅读", "细节题"]}, {"id": "2022-12-1-r-55", "type": "reading", "typeZh": "仔细阅读", "qno": 55, "stem": "What should developing countries do in their future development according to the passage?", "options": ["A) They turn to developed countries for the assistance they need.", "B) They remedy environmental damage by slowing economic growth.", "C) They avoid damaging interference from international institutions.", "D) They improve people's livelihood without harming the environment."], "answer": "D", "analysis": "【答案】D （细节题）\n【判型】题干 What should developing countries do in their future development according to\nthe passage? 明确要 according to the passage，问文中给出的具体建议，是细节题不是\n推断。\n【拆句】What should developing countries do in their future development according to the\npassage? 情态动词疑问句，主干 What should developing countries do，in 短语限定时\n间范围，according to 短语指明答题依据；结构清晰无陷阱。\n【定位】But in developing countries, the path of future development has more potential to change,\nwhich has encouraged international institutions to devise more sustainable growth pathways\nthat are supposed both to alleviate poverty and preserve the environment.\n但在发展中国家，未来发展的路径有更大的可改变潜力，这促使国际机构设计了更可持续的\n发展路径——既要减贫，又要保护环境。\n【选项】A) 无中生有\nturn to developed countries for the assistance they need 说\"向发达国家求援\"，原\n文 P7 只说国际机构\"设计了可持续路径\"，未提向发达国家求援。\nB) 与原文相反\nremedy environmental damage by slowing economic growth 说\"靠放缓经济增长\n来修补环境\"，但原文 P7 提的 sustainable growth pathways 是\"既减贫又护环境\"——\n发展与环保并行，不是减速换环保。\nC) 与原文相反\navoid damaging interference from international institutions 说\"避开国际机构的破\n坏性干预\"，但原文 P7 has encouraged international institutions to devise more\nsustainable growth pathways 中国际机构是建设性角色——选项把它颠倒成\"破\n坏性\"。\nD) ✓ 正确\nalleviate poverty ↔ improve people's livelihood\npreserve the environment ↔ without harming the environment\n预判\"减贫与护环境兼顾\"在 They improve people's livelihood without harming the\nenvironment 中以 improve...without harming 双动作并列承接 both...and 结构，是\nP7 对策句的标准同义改写。", "points": ["仔细阅读", "细节题"]}]});
